al is **not to redesign DevPad**. It is to have Luce establish a hard ground-truth map of what exists, what is running, which terminal belongs to which seat/runtime/project, what is duplicated or stale, and exactly what remains before the Command Center can replace the terminal sprawl.\n\nUse this with Luce:\n\n:::writing{variant=\"document\" id=\"48317\" title=\"Luce — GCE DevPad Command Center Ground-State Reconciliation\"}\n# GCE DEVPAD COMMAND CENTER — GROUND-STATE RECONCILIATION\n\n**Authority:** Don  \n**Verifier:** Luce / Ground Truth  \n**Mode:** READ-FIRST / VERIFY / RECONCILE  \n**Primary Domain:** GCE Stack  \n**Target:** GCE_DevPad_Command_Center  \n**Objective:** Establish the exact current state of DevPad and the shortest verified path from the present multi-terminal environment to one coherent Command Center view.\n\n---\n\n## 1. MISSION\n\nDon currently has too many terminals, runtime sessions, agents, seats, and project processes open simultaneously.\n\nThe immediate operational problem is no longer conceptual architecture.\n\nThe problem is:\n\n**Don cannot reliably tell who is who, which terminal owns what, which runtime is active, which sessions are authoritative, or how close the DevPad Command Center actually is to replacing this fragmented view.**\n\nDevPad is believed to be relatively close to usable.\n\nYour job is to establish ground truth.\n\nDo **not** redesign the system.\n\nDo **not** invent a new architecture.\n\nDo **not** normalize files simply because they look untidy.\n\nDo **not** promote assumptions into current state.\n\nInspect first. Reconstruct what actually exists.\n\n---\n\n# 2. AUTHORITY / ROLE BOUNDARIES\n\nPreserve current GCE doctrine:\n\n- **Don** — Founder / final authority / orchestrator\n- **Coda** — strategic advisor / governance / canon / reconciliation\n- **Luce** — independent verification / ground truth\n- **Vittorio** — technical advisor / warboard / challenge\n- **Chiave** — architecture when materially required\n- **Nico** — implementation hammer / builder\n- **Talon** — operations / routing / coordination / maintenance\n- **Keel** — deployment / operational build support / stability\n- **Falcon** — data acquisition / retrieval\n- **Ragno** — principal consultant / integration / translation when genuinely required\n- **Magpie** — registry / secretary\n- **Pigeon** — transport\n- **Raven** — documentation\n- **Corrado** — quant engine only\n\nCore doctrine:\n\n**IDENTITY != ROLE != LENS != PERSONALITY != AUTHORITY != MODEL**\n\nand:\n\n**MODEL != SEAT**\n\nA terminal, model runtime, CLI, API provider, or process must never be assumed to identify the seat occupying it.\n\n---\n\n# 3. SCOPE OF THIS RECON\n\nInspect the current DevPad / Command Center estate and determine:\n\n### A. What exists\n\nLocate and inventory all current artifacts related to:\n\n- DevPad\n- Command Center\n- GCE command UI\n- agent/seat dashboarding\n- terminal/session aggregation\n- runtime/provider status\n- process monitoring\n- local service management\n- project launch/control\n- seat identity display\n- model/runtime identity display\n- logs/status panes\n- orchestration controls\n- terminal wrappers\n- shells\n- launchers\n- daemon/service components\n- frontend components\n- backend/API components\n- config\n- manifests\n- environment files\n- startup scripts\n- tests\n- build outputs\n- documentation\n- TODOs / handoffs / implementation plans\n\nInclude relevant material under the current GCE Stack and Don operating estate.\n\nDo not assume filenames are consistent.\n\n---\n\n### B. What is actually running\n\nDetermine, as far as safely observable:\n\n- active terminals\n- active shells\n- active local servers\n- active DevPad processes\n- Node / Python / PowerShell / WSL / Git Bash processes associated with the system\n- ports being used\n- background services\n- watchers\n- API bridges\n- runtime/provider bridges\n- Bedrock integrations\n- Kimi integrations\n- OpenAI integrations\n- GLM / ZAI integrations\n- any other provider/runtime currently wired into DevPad\n\nFor each running component, identify where possible:\n\n- process\n- executable\n- working directory\n- project\n- seat\n- model/runtime\n- provider\n- purpose\n- port\n- launch mechanism\n- current state\n- whether it is safe to stop/restart\n- whether it appears duplicate or orphaned\n\nDo **not** terminate anything during recon unless Don separately authorizes it.\n\n---\n\n# 4. TERMINAL IDENTITY RECONCILIATION\n\nThis is a critical deliverable.\n\nCreate a **Terminal / Session Identity Map**.\n\nFor every terminal or long-running runtime session you can identify, return:\n\n| Field | Required |\n|---|---|\n| Terminal / Window identifier | Yes |\n| Shell | Yes |\n| Working directory | Yes |\n| Project / system | Yes |\n| Seat | VERIFIED / INFERRED / UNKNOWN |\n| Model | VERIFIED / INFERRED / UNKNOWN |\n| Provider | VERIFIED / INFERRED / UNKNOWN |\n| Current task | Yes |\n| Parent process | If available |\n| Child processes | If relevant |\n| Port(s) | If relevant |\n| Started from | If discoverable |\n| Still needed? | YES / NO / UNKNOWN |\n| Evidence | Yes |\n| Confidence | Yes |\n\nThe target outcome is that Don can look at the table and answer:\n\n**“What the hell is this terminal, who is in it, and can I close it?”**\n\nIf a terminal cannot be confidently identified, mark:\n\n**UNKNOWN — DO NOT ASSIGN IDENTITY**\n\nDo not infer a seat merely because a specific model CLI is running.\n\n---\n\n# 5. DEVPAD CURRENT IMPLEMENTATION STATE\n\nReconstruct the DevPad build itself.\n\nSeparate findings into:\n\n## IMPLEMENTED + VERIFIED\n\nExists and works based on direct evidence.\n\n## IMPLEMENTED BUT NOT VERIFIED\n\nCode/artifact exists, but execution or integration has not been confirmed.\n\n## PARTIALLY IMPLEMENTED\n\nSome portion exists but required wiring is incomplete.\n\n## DESIGNED / DOCUMENTED ONLY\n\nDefined in plans/docs but not implemented.\n\n## STALE / SUPERSEDED\n\nHistorical implementation no longer part of the current path.\n\n## UNKNOWN\n\nInsufficient evidence.\n\nDo not collapse these categories.\n\n---\n\n# 6. FUNCTIONAL CAPABILITY MATRIX\n\nDetermine current state for at least these capabilities:\n\n| Capability | State | Evidence | Gap |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| One Command Center UI | | | |\n| Terminal/session list | | | |\n| Seat identity display | | | |\n| Model identity display | | | |\n| Provider identity display | | | |\n| Project/workstream identity | | | |\n| Runtime health/status | | | |\n| Start runtime | | | |\n| Stop runtime | | | |\n| Restart runtime | | | |\n| Open terminal | | | |\n| Attach/reconnect to session | | | |\n| Logs/output view | | | |\n| Current-task/status view | | | |\n| Port/process visibility | | | |\n| Local service visibility | | | |\n| Bedrock provider support | | | |\n| Kimi provider support | | | |\n| OpenAI provider support | | | |\n| GLM/ZAI provider support | | | |\n| Project switching | | | |\n| Seat ↔ runtime separation | | | |\n| Persistent session identity | | | |\n| Crash/restart recovery | | | |\n| Config management | | | |\n| Secret isolation | | | |\n| Command history / audit trail | | | |\n| Command Center launch/bootstrap | | | |\n\nAdd capabilities actually present in the implementation even if they are not listed here.\n\n---\n\n# 7. ARCHITECTURE — OBSERVE, DO NOT REDESIGN\n\nReconstruct the **existing implemented architecture** only.\n\nReturn a simple current-state flow such as:\n\n**UI → local API/service → process/session manager → provider/runtime → project filesystem**\n\nBut use the architecture actually present.\n\nIdentify:\n\n- frontend technology\n- backend technology\n- IPC/API mechanism\n- local ports\n- storage/state mechanism\n- process/session manager\n- terminal mechanism\n- runtime adapters\n- config source\n- identity source\n- project registry\n- provider registry\n- log source\n- secret source\n\nExplicitly identify any places where the implementation violates or blurs:\n\n**SEAT vs MODEL vs PROVIDER vs TERMINAL vs PROJECT**\n\nThis is verification, not redesign.\n\n---\n\n# 8. SOURCE / AUTHORITY RECONCILIATION\n\nFor each important DevPad artifact, classify it:\n\n- CURRENT IMPLEMENTATION TRUTH\n- CURRENT SUPPORTING ARTIFACT\n- DESIGN REFERENCE\n- HISTORICAL\n- STALE\n- SUPERSEDED\n- DUPLICATE\n- UNKNOWN\n\nIdentify contradictions between:\n\n- code\n- config\n- documentation\n- handoffs\n- launch scripts\n- current runtime behavior\n\nWhere two sources disagree, report both and identify which one the actual runtime follows.\n\nRuntime behavior and current implementation truth take precedence over stale design notes unless an explicit authority artifact says otherwise.\n\n---\n\n# 9. BUILD / TEST STATE\n\nDetermine:\n\n- whether the frontend builds\n- whether backend/services start\n- current test suites\n- last known test results if evidenced\n- broken tests\n- lint/type errors\n- missing dependencies\n- config failures\n- environment dependencies\n- startup blockers\n- provider connection blockers\n- platform assumptions\n- hardcoded paths\n- hardcoded identities\n- hardcoded ports\n- stale references\n\nDo not repair them unless separately authorized.\n\nThis is a reconnaissance and verification pass.\n\n---\n\n# 10. HOW CLOSE ARE WE?\n\nGive Don a concrete completion assessment without hand-waving.\n\nDo **not** use a made-up percentage unless it can be defended from the implementation.\n\nInstead return:\n\n### Already complete\nSpecific pieces that are genuinely done.\n\n### Remaining before “Don can stop juggling terminals”\nOnly the capabilities required for the Command Center to become operationally useful.\n\n### Remaining after first usable release\nEnhancements that can wait.\n\n### Blockers\nAnything preventing a usable Command Center now.\n\n### Dependencies\nAnything requiring another system, provider, credential, architecture decision, or Don decision.\n\n---\n\n# 11. MINIMUM VIABLE COMMAND CENTER\n\nBased strictly on the existing implementation, identify the **minimum remaining verified slice** required so Don can use DevPad as his primary view.\n\nDo not propose a new product.\n\nAnswer:\n\n**What is the smallest amount of remaining work that gets Don from many unidentified terminals to one reliable operational console?**\n\nSeparate:\n\n- MUST HAVE\n- SHOULD HAVE\n- LATER\n\nKeep MUST HAVE brutally narrow.\n\n---\n\n# 12. DO-NOT-TOUCH BOUNDARY\n\nDuring this pass:\n\n- Do not kill processes.\n- Do not close terminals.\n- Do not change credentials.\n- Do not rotate secrets.\n- Do not modify `.env` files.\n- Do not redesign architecture.\n- Do not rename large directory trees.\n- Do not move authoritative artifacts.\n- Do not delete stale files.\n- Do not rewrite Framework authority.\n- Do not assign seats based solely on runtime/model.\n- Do not modify Google Drive.\n- Do not implement fixes unless Don separately authorizes implementation.\n\nIf you need a command to inspect something, inspection is allowed.\n\nPrefer reversible/read-only inspection.\n\n---\n\n# 13. REQUIRED RETURN\n\nReturn exactly these sections:\n\n## 1. EXECUTIVE GROUND TRUTH\n\nMaximum 15 lines.\n\nTell Don plainly:\n\n- where DevPad actually stands\n- whether the core system exists\n- whether it runs\n- whether one-view consolidation is close\n- what is preventing immediate use\n\n---\n\n## 2. CURRENT DEVPAD ESTATE\n\nImportant directories, files, services, components, and entry points.\n\n---\n\n## 3. LIVE PROCESS / TERMINAL MAP\n\nIdentify every relevant active runtime/session you can safely inspect.\n\nThis section must make the terminal sprawl understandable.\n\n---\n\n## 4. SEAT / MODEL / PROVIDER / PROJECT MAP\n\nKeep these identities separate.\n\nNever flatten them.\n\n---\n\n## 5. IMPLEMENTATION STATUS MATRIX\n\nIMPLEMENTED + VERIFIED / IMPLEMENTED NOT VERIFIED / PARTIAL / DOCUMENTED ONLY / STALE / UNKNOWN.\n\n---\n\n## 6. FUNCTIONAL CAPABILITY MATRIX\n\nUse the capability matrix above and add anything material you discover.\n\n---\n\n## 7. CURRENT ARCHITECTURE\n\nObserved architecture only.\n\nNo redesign.\n\n---\n\n## 8. BUILD + TEST STATE\n\nWhat starts, builds, passes, fails, or is unknown.\n\n---\n\n## 9. CONTRADICTIONS / STALE REFERENCES\n\nAnything likely to confuse Don or another agent.\n\n---\n\n## 10. BLOCKERS\n\nActual blockers only.\n\n---\n\n## 11. MINIMUM REMAINING SLICE\n\nThe narrowest path to:\n\n**ONE VIEW → IDENTIFIED SESSIONS → IDENTIFIED SEATS/RUNTIMES → BASIC CONTROL**\n\n---\n\n## 12. SAFE TERMINAL CLEANUP CANDIDATES\n\nFor each candidate:\n\n- process/session\n- why it appears unnecessary\n- confidence\n- evidence\n- whether Don can likely close it\n\nDo **not** close it yourself.\n\n---\n\n## 13. UNKNOWN / NEEDS DON\n\nOnly decisions that genuinely require Don.\n\nDo not send Don questions that can be answered by inspecting the estate.\n\n---\n\n## 14. FINAL LUCE VERDICT\n\nReturn one of:\n\n- **GROUND VERIFIED — READY FOR IMPLEMENTATION**\n- **GROUND VERIFIED — MINOR BLOCKERS**\n- **GROUND VERIFIED — MATERIAL BLOCKERS**\n- **GROUND NOT YET ESTABLISHED**\n\nThen provide no more than **5 next actions**, in dependency order.\n\n---\n\n# OPERATING PRINCIPLE\n\nThe goal is not architectural elegance.\n\nThe goal is to make it possible for Don to open the GCE DevPad Command Center and immediately know:\n\n**Who is running?  \nWhat model are they using?  \nWhat provider is underneath them?  \nWhat project are they working on?  \nWhat are they doing?  \nAre they alive?  \nCan Don open, stop, restart, or reconnect to them?**\n\nRight now terminal sprawl is creating operational ambiguity.\n\nYour job is to turn that ambiguity into verified ground truth so the existing DevPad build can be finished instead of redesigned.\n:::\n\nThat should force Luce to **inventory first and stop anybody from accidentally turning this into DevPad v7 architecture theater**. The most valuable output will probably be the **live terminal/session identity map + minimum remaining slice**—those two pieces tell us whether Nico/Keel can finish this quickly. memcite"]}, "create_time": 1790217762.227572, "end_turn": true, "id": "ed5f53b1-cf7a-4e57-baf3-ed1faadb453a", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "content_references": [{"alt": null, "end_idx": 13574, "invalid": false, "matched_text": "memcite", "prefix": null, "prompt_text": null, "refs": [], "safe_urls": [], "start_idx": 13565, "type": "hidden"}], "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finish_details": {"stop_tokens": [200002], "type": "stop"}, "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab41b7c2620819187c626358eeb8a48", "is_complete": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "8274f4da-0e0e-4941-b356-c1938f2b107d", "request_id": "2b15c8a3-fe02-42bd-b7d2-dee02b2aab25", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "search_result_groups": [], "story_events": [], "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "c20cf314-9d2d-4288-8767-5392a2c5ff3d", "working_turn_id": "c20cf314-9d2d-4288-8767-5392a2c5ff3d"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790217887.396723, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content_type": "model_editable_context", "model_set_context": "", "repo_summary": null, "repository": null, "structured_context": null}, "create_time": 1790217762.2331126, "end_turn": null, "id": "2b03ccc7-98af-41a3-98ff-e48db701f37a", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "chime_version": 1, "classifier_response": "default", "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab41b7c2620819187c626358eeb8a48", "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "1cc667fa-6669-4def-8aab-ebd92069f9df", "reasoning_start_