ype": "text", "parts": [""]}, "create_time": 1790218112.878694, "end_turn": null, "id": "05467d0c-57d7-4a4f-a7fa-8a797056f81a", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "chime_version": 1, "classifier_response": "default", "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab41b7c2620819187c626358eeb8a48", "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "parent_id": "945ef670-fc10-4983-8a21-41198db5d2d8", "reasoning_start_time": 1790218111.2143342, "reasoning_status": "is_reasoning", "reasoning_title": "Searching best Snapdragon 8 Elite phones 16GB RAM global US bands 2026 OnePlus Xiaomi Poco RedMagic Asus ROG Honor Motorola", "reasoning_titles": ["Searching best Snapdragon 8 Elite phones 16GB RAM global US bands 2026 OnePlus Xiaomi Poco RedMagic Asus ROG Honor Motorola"], "request_id": "5355d2ac-cdba-428a-993d-d5e9301b4e2d", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "search_model_queries": {"queries": ["best Snapdragon 8 Elite phones 16GB RAM global US bands 2026 OnePlus Xiaomi Poco RedMagic Asus ROG Honor Motorola"], "type": "search_model_queries"}, "thinking_effort": "standard", "tool_icons": ["globe"], "turn_exchange_id": "2a1ede85-ed60-4b60-ab15-e2051156ec7d", "working_turn_id": "2a1ede85-ed60-4b60-ab15-e2051156ec7d"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {"real_author": "tool:web"}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Yeah — there **are** outside contenders, but once you remove Pixel, Galaxy, and iPhone, the field gets much more interesting.\n\nFor your **GCE Stack phone** criteria — **Snapdragon first, RAM second, battery/thermals third, camera irrelevant** — these are the brands I’d keep in the audition pool:\n\n- **OnePlus** — still the easiest U.S. enthusiast option.\n- **Xiaomi / POCO** — probably the best “hardware per dollar” lane, especially POCO. Xiaomi 15/17 and POCO F-series give you Snapdragon 8 Elite-class silicon with 16 GB configurations. Qualcomm’s own device finder confirms Xiaomi 15, OnePlus 13, ROG Phone 9, and RedMagic 10 on Snapdragon 8 Elite. citeturn470164search5turn470164search6\n- **REDMAGIC / Nubia** — very relevant for you. These are basically **compute/gaming appliances disguised as phones**: big RAM, aggressive cooling, large batteries. REDMAGIC 10-series uses Snapdragon 8 Elite, and the newer REDMAGIC 11 line pushes the same performance-first philosophy further. citeturn470164search0turn470164news13\n- **ASUS ROG Phone** — absolutely an outside contender. Snapdragon flagship silicon, huge battery, thermal headroom, lots of RAM. The downside is that it often costs **more than OnePlus**, which undermines the value argument. citeturn470164search1turn470164news13\n- **Realme GT** — sleeper option. The GT 7 Pro is another Snapdragon 8 Elite performance-oriented device, but U.S. carrier/support logistics are more import-heavy. citeturn470164search0\n- **iQOO** — Vivo’s performance/gaming sub-brand. The iQOO 13 is Snapdragon 8 Elite and is built much more around performance/value than camera prestige. Again, U.S. compatibility/import support is the catch. citeturn470164search0turn470164search2\n- **Motorola** — worth remembering because it has better U.S. network compatibility than most Chinese imports. But its highest-end Snapdragon phones tend to be foldables or premium-priced, so it’s less aligned with your “give me compute, not jewelry” objective. citeturn470164search0\n\nThe one I’d add **immediately** to our shortlist is **REDMAGIC**. It fits your philosophy almost absurdly well: **Snapdragon + lots of RAM + cooling + huge battery, with less money wasted chasing camera supremacy**.\n\nAnd there’s a funny inversion here: the old OnePlus ethos you liked — *flagship killer, maximum silicon for the money* — now arguably lives more in **POCO, REDMAGIC, Realme, and iQOO** than in OnePlus itself.\n\nSo our exploratory **GCE Mobile compute shortlist** is now:\n\n**OnePlus 13R / older OnePlus flagship → POCO F-series → REDMAGIC → Xiaomi base flagship → Realme GT / iQOO as import wildcards.**\n\nI’d probably investigate **REDMAGIC vs POCO next**, because that is the purest test of your requirement: *“I don’t give a shit about the camera; how much Snapdragon and RAM can I get for my money?”*"]}, "create_time": 1790218119.052032, "end_turn": true, "id": "d6773b6b-2593-4594-b570-0b253257770c", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "content_references": [{"alt": "([Qualcomm](https://www.qualcomm.com/smartphones/device-finder?utm_source=chatgpt.com))", "end_idx": 696, "error": null, "fallback_items": null, "items": [{"attribution": "Qualcomm", "attribution_segments": null, "attributions": null, "hue": null, "pub_date": null, "refs": [{"ref_index": 5, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 0}, {"ref_index": 6, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 0}], "snippet": "", "supporting_websites": [{"attribution": "Qualcomm", "pub_date": null, "snippet": "", "title": "Discover Your Perfect Snapdragon Device: Smartphones, Tablets & Laptops", "url": "https://www.qualcomm.com/snapdragon/device-finder?deviceApplication=Smartphone&utm_source=chatgpt.com"}], "title": "Smartphone Device Finder | Qualcomm", "url": "https://www.qualcomm.com/smartphones/device-finder?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}], "matched_text": "citeturn470164search5turn470164search6", "prefix": null, "prompt_text": null, "refs": [], "safe_urls": ["https://www.qualcomm.com/smartphones/device-finder", "https://www.qualcomm.com/smartphones/device-finder?utm_source=chatgpt.com", "https://www.qualcomm.com/snapdragon/device-finder?deviceApplication=Smartphone", "https://www.qualcomm.com/snapdragon/device-finder?deviceApplication=Smartphone&utm_source=chatgpt.com"], "start_idx": 654, "status": "done", "style": null, "type": "grouped_webpages"}, {"alt": "([CloudsPress](https://www.cloudspress.com/all-snapdragon-8-elite-phones