6.782858, "end_turn": false, "id": "b63c7777-b25f-471d-bea5-f0d001eddd3c", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "classifier_response": "default", "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "hide_inline_actions": true, "inline_cot_expandable_content": {"search_result_groups": [{"domain": "www.tomsguide.com", "entries": [{"attribution": "www.tomsguide.com", "pub_date": 1789991983, "ref_id": {"ref_index": 12, "ref_type": "news", "turn_index": 470164}, "snippet": "In 2026, the top smartphones have been rigorously tested and rated on performance, camera quality, battery life, and price. The Apple iPhone 18 Pro Max emerges as the best overall phone, boasting a new variable aperture camera, A20 Pro chip, and improved 18.5-hour battery life, though it commands a high price starting at $1,299. For Android users, the Samsung Galaxy S26 Ultra is the best, featuring superior zoom, a 200MP main camera, and innovative privacy display, priced similarly to Apple's flagship. \n\nFor budget users, the $499 Google Pixel 10a offers excellent value with solid camera performance, durable design, and long battery life. Gamers and power users seeking top battery longevity should consider the Asus ROG Phone 9 Pro, which lasts over 20 hours but comes at a hefty $1,100. The Google Pixel 10 and iPhone 17 provide strong flagship performance at a more accessible $799, with the former excelling in AI tools and camera upgrades and the latter narrowing the gap with Apple’s Pro models. Samsung's Galaxy Z Fold 8 Ultra leads the foldable category with improved design and internals, despite its steep $2,099 starting price.", "thumbnail_url": "https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/LZzLtLtUOxth1ZaxA8bESin0OyBQdMO--5ncK63C3DU6JyZGoSs4flRbfBVl62uxUqpC1rYrGRUVHYrgDuhxOka6-DoE3h6yyGVtGT-_76sM2rG4hC_bu9y0fKOSfcVF", "title": "Best phones 2026 tested - our top picks", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://www.tomsguide.com/best-picks/best-phones"}, {"attribution": "www.tomsguide.com", "pub_date": 1790007623, "ref_id": {"ref_index": 13, "ref_type": "news", "turn_index": 470164}, "snippet": "As of 2026, gaming phones offer powerful alternatives to consoles and PCs, providing robust performance, long battery life, and high-refresh-rate displays for immersive gameplay. The Asus ROG Phone 9 Pro tops the list as the best overall gaming phone, with a 185Hz AMOLED display, Snapdragon 8 Elite chipset, exceptional 20:34 battery life, and gaming-specific features like AirTrigger controls and AniMe lights. For Android users wanting a flagship device with strong gaming credentials, the Samsung Galaxy S26 Ultra delivers with excellent GPU performance, efficient cooling, and powerful cameras. Meanwhile, the iPhone 18 Pro Max is the best gaming iPhone, offering the A20 Pro chip and impressive battery life, though with a heftier price tag. For value-conscious gamers, the RedMagic 11 Pro brings liquid and fan cooling and top-tier specs at a lower cost, albeit with weaker camera and dust resistance. Finally, the Galaxy Z Fold 7 offers a unique foldable experience with a large display and high-end internals, though at $2,000 it overdelivers for pure gaming needs. Overall, the best choice depends on user priorities such as OS, performance, budget, and additional features like photography or portability.", "thumbnail_url": "https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/xvgt11_XzzNZeyHhu5Lj-DxlC_6Yrle0ziEQVVMl4YTYLXtF4yNp5uNLRrFXT_1KkFypUFpaUxAjcinMdZm62JOq29XeikM0OCHSKMSDfprDaQM0YHd0uar_HUfQ1K7f", "title": "The best gaming phone 2026 - I tested them all to crown a winner", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://www.tomsguide.com/best-picks/best-gaming-phones"}, {"attribution": "www.tomsguide.com", "pub_date": 1790003659, "ref_id": {"ref_index": 14, "ref_type": "news", "turn_index": 470164}, "snippet": "If you're in the market for a large smartphone, this guide highlights the best big phones of 2026, ideal for users who prioritize spacious displays, extended battery life, and top-tier performance. The best overall is the Samsung Galaxy S26 Ultra, boasting a 6.9-inch AMOLED screen, Snapdragon 8 Elite Gen 5 chip, and robust features like customizable privacy and AI tools. It stands out for exceptional performance and camera quality, despite minor drawbacks like its large camera bump.\n\nFor Apple fans, the iPhone 18 Pro Max also features a 6.9-inch display, A20 Pro chip, and superior battery life (18:27 hours), making it the top choice among big iPhones. It shines with strong performance, advanced camera capabilities, and fast charging, albeit with a higher price and heftier build.\n\nIf you're seeking flexibility, the foldable Motorola Razr Fold offers an expansive 8.1-inch inner screen and strong multitasking abilities. It supports up to four simultaneous apps and delivers solid battery life despite a few software hiccups.\n\nUltimately, Android offers more diversity in design and features, while iPhones provide tight ecosystem integration. Benchmarks and battery tests confirm these devices deliver premium user experiences for gaming, media, and productivity.", "thumbnail_url": "https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/c3RjLnoMopdwAR7JSTKEQAroMG5Ml72IfIJ_ROIgCkkydxftNUcV5Dqmdh0CsUJ-UfBpg8hwnO3Brvqm1wAoMeImIgFvJhBxSo5fxZEfCB272Fi5l4x7EextOV9PvLDq", "title": "I love big phones and I cannot lie - and here are the best you can buy right now", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://www.tomsguide.com/best-picks/best-big-phones"}, {"attribution": "www.tomsguide.com", "pub_date": 1789628400, "ref_id": {"ref_index": 16, "ref_type": "news", "turn_index": 470164}, "snippet": "The Tom's Guide Awards 2026 highlights the top smartphones of the past year across various categories, based on thorough testing and evaluations. The iPhone 18 Pro and Pro Max were crowned Best Phone for their powerhouse A20 Pro chip, advanced variable-aperture camera, and improved Siri features. Samsung dominated in multiple categories with the Galaxy S26 Ultra, winning Best Android Phone and Best Camera Phone due to its versatile quad-camera setup and professional-grade videography tools. Google Pixel 11 Pro XL earned Best AI Phone for its leading-edge AI features powered by the Tensor G6 chip, including tools like \"Rambler\" and Magic Capture. The Galaxy Z Fold 8 was named Best Foldable thanks to its redesigned wide-screen format and elite multitasking capabilities. Best Battery Life went to the OnePlus 15, boasting over 25 hours of usage and revolutionary Silicon Carbon battery technology. Lastly, the Nothing Phone 4a Pro won Best Budget Phone, offering flagship-level features and unique design elements like the Glyph Matrix at an affordable price point.", "thumbnail_url": "https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/-h_2GZJOL9xjg_vN-oWqXuoaVIMYCf8eqpDevmPhJBomNvaUHbk-MYLO52CxZSAKaY_6UGMM2fNZ9WdlbNSh_P8cPDJWby-lIm69vslilRoTAFmKHI7kNQbE9DPNq9yy", "title": "Tom's Guide Awards 2026: Our favorite phones of the year", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://www.tomsguide.com/phones/toms-guide-awards-2026"}], "type": "search_result_group"}, {"domain": "www.androidcentral.com", "entries": [{"attribution": "www.androidcentral.com", "pub_date": 1789677288, "ref_id": {"ref_index": 15, "ref_type": "news", "turn_index": 470164}, "snippet": "In 2026, flagship Android smartphones have significantly improved in water resistance, with devices now often earning IP68 or IP69 certifications for protection against water and dust. The top pick this year is the OnePlus 15, offering an IP69 rating, excellent gaming and camera performance, a large 7,300mAh battery, and competitive pricing at around $900. Budget-conscious buyers can opt for the Moto G Power 2026, which also features IP69 certification for under $300. Samsung’s Galaxy S26 Ultra remains the premium choice with advanced AI features, Privacy Display, and stellar overall performance. The Google Pixel 11 Pro leads in photography with powerful AI tools a