d": "4cfcb63f-2f80-4c30-8a54-cf027f0e2053", "reasoning_start_time": 1790218179.8779252, "reasoning_status": "is_reasoning", "reasoning_title": "Searching REDMAGIC 10 Pro price US official 16GB 512GB 2026", "reasoning_titles": ["Searching REDMAGIC 10 Pro price US official 16GB 512GB 2026", "Searching REDMAGIC 11 Pro price US official 2026", "Searching realme GT 7 Pro price global 16GB 512GB 2026", "Searching realme GT 8 Pro price global 16GB 512GB 2026"], "request_id": "30cc6759-4ec8-4637-8411-c4031fc706b6", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "search_model_queries": {"queries": ["REDMAGIC 10 Pro price US official 16GB 512GB 2026", "REDMAGIC 11 Pro price US official 2026", "realme GT 7 Pro price global 16GB 512GB 2026", "realme GT 8 Pro price global 16GB 512GB 2026"], "type": "search_model_queries"}, "thinking_effort": "standard", "tool_icons": ["globe"], "turn_exchange_id": "93c14cf3-16f2-4e99-a446-ef30cfc272df", "working_turn_id": "93c14cf3-16f2-4e99-a446-ef30cfc272df"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {"real_author": "tool:web"}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Yes — **now we’re in the interesting lane.** And quick correction: it’s **REDMAGIC**, not Red Dragon. Nubia makes it.\n\nFor your criteria — **Snapdragon, RAM, battery, thermals, cellular plan compatibility, camera irrelevant** — REDMAGIC is probably the most “GCE phone” thing on the market.\n\nproducts{\"selections\":[[\"turn277714product3\",\"REDMAGIC 11 Pro\"],[\"turn277714product2\",\"realme GT 7 Pro 16GB/512GB\"],[\"turn277714product4\",\"realme GT 8 Pro 16GB/512GB\"],[\"turn277714product1\",\"REDMAGIC 10 Pro 16GB/512GB\"]]}\n\n### The two I’d focus on\n\n**REDMAGIC 11 Pro** is the cleaner performance-first choice. Official launch pricing was **$699 for 12/256, $799 for 16/512, and $999 for 24GB/1TB**. That is exactly the sort of RAM ladder we want. citeturn277714search2\n\nThe older **REDMAGIC 10 Pro** used Snapdragon 8 Elite, offered **16GB/512GB and even 24GB/1TB**, had a **7,050 mAh battery**, active/liquid-metal cooling, and originally started around $649. REDMAGIC now lists it as discontinued/out of stock, so I would only buy one if the secondary-market price were excellent. citeturn277714search1\n\n**realme GT 7 Pro** is the sleeper value candidate. The global model has **Snapdragon 8 Elite, up to 16GB/512GB, LPDDR5X, UFS 4.0, a 6,500 mAh battery and 120W charging**. I’m seeing a 16/512 listing around **$669**, which is extremely interesting. citeturn277714search0turn277714search6\n\n### REDMAGIC vs Realme for Don\n\n| | **REDMAGIC 11 Pro** | **Realme GT 7 Pro** |\n|---|---|---|\n| Philosophy | Gaming/compute appliance | Normal flagship with performance focus |\n| RAM sweet spot | **16GB**, even 24GB available | **16GB** max |\n| Snapdragon | Flagship Snapdragon | **8 Elite** |\n| Cooling | **Major emphasis / active cooling** | Conventional flagship cooling |\n| Battery | Huge | **6500 mAh** |\n| Charging | Fast | **120W** |\n| Everyday-phone vibe | Aggressive gamer hardware | Much more normal |\n| GCE fit | **Maximum sustained compute** | Excellent compute + normal daily driver |\n| US ownership risk | Moderate | Higher/import-oriented |\n\nThe **Realme GT 8 Pro** is newer and technically wild: **Snapdragon 8 Elite Gen 5, 16GB/512GB, 7,000 mAh, 120W charging, 50W wireless and a 144Hz QHD+ display**. But current import pricing I'm seeing around **$894+** largely destroys the value proposition. citeturn277714search3turn277714product4\n\n### The part we need to investigate hard: cellular\n\nThis is where I would **not buy blindly**.\n\nThe global Realme GT 7 Pro supports LTE **2/4/5/12/13/17/66** and 5G **n2/n5/n41/n66/n77**, among others. That's useful U.S. spectrum, but notably its published global list does **not show n71**, which matters for T-Mobile's long-range 5G footprint. citeturn277714search0\n\nREDMAGIC actually publishes a carrier-compatibility checker on its product pages and explicitly warns that supporting frequencies does **not guarantee activation if a carrier hasn't approved the device**. That's exactly the issue we'd need to validate before putting money down. citeturn277714search1turn277714search7\n\nSo my exploratory ranking for **your actual use case** is:\n\n**REDMAGIC 11 Pro 16/512** — first thing I'd investigate seriously.  \n**Realme GT 7 Pro 16/512** — potential value monster around $650–700.  \n**REDMAGIC 11 Pro 24GB/1TB** — hilarious and legitimately useful if we start doing heavier local AI/Termux work.  \n**Realme GT 8 Pro** — technically awesome, but not at ~$900–1,000+.\n\nAnd here's the interesting threshold: **$799 for 16GB/512GB REDMAGIC isn't cheap-old-OnePlus money, but it is far closer to a portable workstation than a normal flagship phone.** If the cellular compatibility checks out on T-Mobile, I would take that much more seriously than paying similar money for camera-centric mainstream flagships.\n\nNext thing I'd dig into is **REDMAGIC 11 Pro U.S./T-Mobile bands, VoLTE/Wi-Fi calling, bootloader/ADB/Termux friendliness, desktop-mode possibilities, and whether 24GB RAM actually gives us anything meaningful for local GCE tooling.** That's where this gets fun."]}, "create_time": 1790218183.430759, "end_turn": true, "id": "4705cd37-023b-4e7f-a58e-020b8ab435bb", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "content_references": [{"alt": "### [REDMAGIC 11 Pro](https://ha2ajk-qu.myshopify.com/products/red-magic-11-pro-gaming-phone?utm_campaign=openai_catalog&utm_content=product_card&utm_medium=feed&variant=48988455928057&utm_source=chatgpt.com)\n*$712.44*\n\n### [realme GT 7 Pro 16GB/512GB](https://www.newegg.com/p/23B-00G6-001J9?item=9SIBK15KSG0596&negg_topt=1015&utm_campaign=ais_openai_product_feed&utm_medium=ai_search&utm_source=chatgpt.com)\n*$669.39*\n\n### [realme GT 8 Pro 16GB/512GB](https://ave