7-9f50-8af664ea8de1", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "status": "running", "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "6b573af3-f8db-4e63-9d1c-bc5000dc2aa2", "working_turn_id": "6b573af3-f8db-4e63-9d1c-bc5000dc2aa2"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 0}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Yes. **Keep MiMo. Change the seat, not the model.** That is actually a useful test of the doctrine: MiMo just performed the Luce verification pass; now you reload it under the **Nico bootstrap** and explicitly hand it an implementation contract. **MODEL != SEAT.**\n\nAnd Luce gave us enough. The key finding is that the Command Center already exists and is substantially implemented; it simply is **not running**, while the live OpenCode/Kimi terminals are operating outside it. fileciteturn1file0L5-L16 The minimum slice Luce identified is also clean: boot it, add a read-only process/session inventory, expose model/provider/CWD while leaving seat UNKNOWN when it cannot be proven, and fix the stale launcher. fileciteturn1file0L177-L189\n\nSo after MiMo loads the **Nico bootstrap**, give it this:\n\n> **GCE DEVPAD COMMAND CENTER — NICO IMPLEMENTATION SLICE**\n>\n> **Authority:** Don  \n> **Seat:** Nico  \n> **Runtime/model:** Runtime-declared — MODEL != SEAT  \n> **Upstream verification:** Luce ground-state reconciliation, 2026-09-23  \n> **Mode:** IMPLEMENT / VERIFY / MINIMUM SLICE  \n> **Primary target:** `GCE_DON\\command-center\\`\n>\n> ## Mission\n>\n> Luce has completed ground-state reconciliation.\n>\n> **Do not redesign DevPad.**\n>\n> The canonical GCE Command Center already exists at:\n>\n> `GCE_DON\\command-center\\`\n>\n> It is currently down. The immediate objective is to turn the existing implementation into a usable primary operational view for Don with the **smallest safe implementation slice possible**.\n>\n> Desired outcome:\n>\n> **ONE VIEW → LIVE SESSIONS → MODEL/PROVIDER/PROJECT IDENTITY → SEAT WHEN VERIFIED → BASIC OPERATIONAL VISIBILITY**\n>\n> We are solving Don's terminal-sprawl problem, not building a new platform.\n>\n> ---\n>\n> ## Luce-established ground truth\n>\n> Treat these as the starting facts:\n>\n> - Existing Command Center: Node HTTP/WebSocket + xterm.js + node-pty + seat registry + adapters.\n> - Normal port: `4727`.\n> - Command Center is **not currently running**.\n> - Existing external runtime estate includes:\n>   - 3 OpenCode TUIs\n>   - 1 Kimi CLI\n>   - inbox MCP children\n>   - VoiceBridge\n> - Those existing TUIs were not launched by DevPad and therefore must **not** be assigned seats by inference.\n> - Current OpenCode session metadata exposes runtime/session information but does not reliably encode seat identity.\n> - `runtime-state.json` is presently absent.\n> - OS process/port inventory is presently missing from DevPad.\n> - Existing `Tools\\shortcuts\\Command Center.lnk` points to a stale/missing path.\n> - Historical BOM/config launch failure appears corrected in current code but must be re-tested rather than assumed fixed.\n>\n> ---\n>\n> # PHASE 0 — PRESERVE CURRENT WORK\n>\n> **Do not kill, restart, close, adopt, attach to, or mutate any existing OpenCode/Kimi terminal.**\n>\n> Existing work may be active.\n>\n> Do not rotate credentials.\n>\n> Do not inspect secret values.\n>\n> Do not touch unrelated projects.\n>\n> Do not modify ECQ Quant DevPad. It is a separate application.\n>\n> Do not refactor the Command Center architecture.\n>\n> Before edits, capture:\n>\n> - current git/repo status if applicable\n> - files you expect to touch\n> - current relevant PIDs\n> - current listeners on DevPad-related ports\n>\n> ---\n>\n> # PHASE 1 — PROVE THE EXISTING COMMAND CENTER\n>\n> Start with the implementation already on disk.\n>\n> 1. Inspect:\n>    - `server.js`\n>    - `start-devpad.cmd`\n>    - `config.json`\n>    - `seats.js`\n>    - `adapter.js`\n>    - relevant adapters\n>    - `public/index.html`\n>    - `public/renderer.js`\n>    - `public/styles.css`\n>\n> 2. Run existing syntax/build checks appropriate to this project.\n>\n> 3. Start the Command Center using its intended launcher.\n>\n> 4. Verify:\n>    - listener on `:4727`\n>    - UI loads\n>    - `/api/seats`\n>    - existing board renders\n>    - WebSocket path works\n>    - VoiceBridge status endpoint works\n>    - existing panes do not immediately crash\n>\n> 5. Re-test one safe seat-launch path sufficiently to determine whether the historical BOM/config issue is actually resolved.\n>\n> If existing code fails, **repair only the failure necessary to establish this baseline**.\n>\n> Do not proceed into broad cleanup.\n>\n> ---\n>\n> # PHASE 2 — ADD READ-ONLY LIVE PROCESS / SESSION INVENTORY\n>\n> Implement the smallest practical inventory surface inside the existing Command Center.\n>\n> Add a **read-only backend endpoint** that discovers relevant live processes.\n>\n> Minimum fields where observable:\n>\n> - PID\n> - process/executable\n> - parent PID\n> - command line\n> - working directory\n> - listening port(s)\n> - runtime type\n> - OpenCode/Kimi/session identifier if available\n> - model if directly observable\n> - provider if directly observable\n> - project/CWD if directly observable\n> - seat\n> - confidence/source\n>\n> Seat handling is binding:\n>\n> **If seat identity is not directly established, display `UNKNOWN`.**\n>\n> Never derive:\n>\n> `MiMo → Luce`\n>\n> `Kimi → Ragno`\n>\n> `GLM → Chiave`\n>\n> or any equivalent model-to-seat shortcut.\n>\n> **MODEL != SEAT.**\n>\n> Preserve that separation in both backend representation and UI.\n>\n> Prefer read-only OS/session inspection.\n>\n> Do not require elevated privileges unless absolutely necessary.\n>\n> If Windows refuses a process CWD, return:\n>\n> `UNKNOWN`\n>\n> rather than failing the entire inventory.\n>\n> ---\n>\n> # PHASE 3 — ADD THE MINIMAL UI\n>\n> Add one simple operational surface to the existing Command Center.\n>\n> It can be a pane, drawer, table, or existing-layout-compatible component.\n>\n> Do **not** redesign the UI.\n>\n> It must make the external OpenCode/Kimi estate visible.\n>\n> Minimum presentation:\n>\n> **STATUS | SEAT | RUNTIME | MODEL | PROVIDER | PROJECT/CWD | PID | PORT**\n>\n> For example:\n>\n> `LIVE | UNKNOWN | OpenCode | mimo-v2.6-flash-free | openrouter/big-pickle | C:\\...\\ | 19748 | —`\n>\n> Exact values must come from observation, not this example.\n>\n> Don must be able to answer:\n>\n> - What is alive?\n> - What executable/runtime is it?\n> - What model is it using?\n> - What provider supplies it?\n> - What project/CWD is associated with it?\n> - Which seat owns it, if actually known?\n> - Which sessions remain unidentified?\n>\n> Add manual refresh or safe periodic refresh using the simplest existing pattern.\n>\n> No kill buttons yet unless that capability already exists safely and requires no redesign.\n>\n> **Visibility comes before control.**\n>\n> ---\n>\n> # PHASE 4 — PERSISTENCE ONLY IF SMALL\n>\n> Inspect the existing `runtime-state.json` design/path.\n>\n> If persistence can be restored/implemented cleanly without expanding scope, persist only useful runtime identity/status state.\n>\n> Do not allow persisted state to convert prior inference into current truth.\n>\n> A stale PID/session must visibly become stale/offline.\n>\n> If this is not a very small change, defer it and report it.\n>\n> ---\n>\n> # PHASE 5 — FIX THE ENTRY POINT\n>\n> Inspect:\n>\n> `Tools\\shortcuts\\Command Center.lnk`\n>\n> It currently points to a dead historical path.\n>\n> If safely possible, repoint it to the canonical Command Center launcher:\n>\n> `GCE_DON\\command-center\\start-devpad.cmd`\n>\n> If Windows shortcut editing is unreliable or unsafe in the current tooling, do not hack around it.\n>\n> Instead provide Don the exact verified correction required.\n>\n> Do not create competing launchers.\n>\n> ---\n>\n> # PHASE 6 — VERIFICATION\n>\n> After implementation, independently verify:\n>\n> 1. DevPad launches normally.\n> 2. Port `4727` is listening.\n> 3. Browser UI renders.\n> 4. Existing seat board still renders.\n> 5. Existing VoiceBridge integration still works.\n> 6. Process/session inventory endpoint responds.\n> 7. Current OpenCode/Kimi processes appear.\n> 8. Model/provider/project fields populate where evidence exists.\n> 9. Unknown seat identity remains explicitly UNKNOWN.\n> 10. No external TUI was terminated or modified.\n> 11. No unrelated project was changed.\n> 12. Restarting/reloading DevPad does not destroy external sessions.\n>\n> Run existing relevant tests/checks plus narrow tests for new behavior.\n>\n> ---\n>\n> # STOP CONDITIONS\n>\n> Stop and return to Don rather than redesigning if:\n>\n> - reliable external process enumeration requires materially new architecture;\n> - attaching/focusing existing terminal windows requires invasive terminal ownership changes;\n> - seat identity requires guessing;\n> - you discover a second supposedly canonical Command Center;\n> - the current code materially contradicts Luce's ground truth;\n> - fixing the existing implementation expands beyond a narrow patch;\n> - a credential or authority decision is required.\n>\n> ---\n>\n> # SPECIFIC NON-GOALS\n>\n> **Do not implement now:**\n>\n> - ECQ integration\n> - new board/gate architecture\n> - Bedrock retest controls\n> - provider-management redesign\n> - centralized log architecture\n> - full crash recovery\n> - major UI redesign\n> - terminal multiplexing redesign\n> - generalized orchestration framework\n> - seat doctrine changes\n>\n> Those are later.\n>\n> ---\n>\n> # REQUIRED RETURN TO DON\n>\n> Return:\n>\n> ## 1. RESULT\n> `PASS / PARTIAL / BLOCKED`\n>\n> ## 2. WHAT CHANGED\n> Exact files changed and purpose.\n>\n> ## 3. COMMAND CENTER STATE\n> URL/port and whether it is currently operational.\n>\n> ## 4. LIVE INVENTORY RESULT\n> Number/types of relevant sessions detected and what identity fields are now visible.\n>\n> ## 5. SEAT IDENTITY\n> Which sessions are VERIFIED seats versus UNKNOWN.\n>\n> ## 6. VERIFICATION\n> Commands/tests run and results.\n>\n> ## 7. DON ACTION REQUIRED\n> Only genuinely human decisions, especially manual seat mapping.\n>\n> ## 8. DEFERRED\n> Anything intentionally left outside this minimum slice.\n>\n> ## 9. VERDICT\n> One of:\n>\n> - **DEVPAD PRIMARY VIEW READY**\n> - **DEVPAD PRIMARY VIEW READY — MANUAL SEAT MAP REMAINS**\n> - **DEVPAD FUNCTIONAL — MATERIAL GAP REMAINS**\n> - **BLOCKED**\n>\n> ---\n>\n> ## Governing objective\n>\n> Do the **least work necessary** to get Don out of terminal blindness.\n>\n> **Do not build the final Command Center. Make the existing Command Center useful tonight.**\n\n### One thing I would **not** make Don do first\n\nLuce said Don should map the four TUIs before implementation. fileciteturn1file0L203-L216 I would invert that slightly.\n\nHave Nico **surface all four as `UNKNOWN` first**. Then Don can look at one Command Center screen and identify them. That's the whole reason we're building the fucking thing.\n\nSo the sequence becomes:\n\n**MiMo → load Nico → paste prompt → boot existing DevPad → add live inventory → Don maps UNKNOWN sessions → then clean up terminals.**\n\nThat's actionable. No architecture committee required. memcite"]}, "create_time": 1790218576.040819, "end_turn": true, "id": "1cfef4f8-dbd4-422b-a6ff-26b1d9f0efe3", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [{"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 506, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "files/context_stuff", "authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "82328b89-f6ca-4008-ad28-83ad65736d2e", "cited_message_idx": 103, "cloud_doc_url": null, "doi": null, "effective_time": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_b618a934c9748191a6553ca2cd9b8163", "line_range": [5, 16], "publicatio