iceBridge |\n| **6** | Luce |\n| **7** | Talon |\n| **8** | Keel |\n| **9** | Falcon |\n\nThen VoiceBridge can understand commands like **“number 3”**, **“open 6”**, **“focus 2”**, or later **“send this to 7.”**\n\nGive Nico/Big Pickle this small additive patch:\n\n```text\nGCE DEVPAD — STABLE TILE NUMBER / VOICEBRIDGE IDENTITY PATCH\n\nAuthority: Don\nSeat: Nico\nMode: SMALL ADDITIVE PATCH\nTarget: Existing DevPad 3×3 grid\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nAdd a permanent numeric address to every DevPad tile so Don can control/focus terminals through VoiceBridge using simple commands such as:\n\n\"number 1\"\n\"number 2\"\n\"focus 6\"\n\"open number 7\"\n\nThis is an address/alias layer.\n\nIt does NOT replace seat identity.\n\nPreserve:\n\nTILE NUMBER != SEAT != MODEL != RUNTIME\n\n────────────────────────────\nBINDING — FIXED\n────────────────────────────\n\nUse row-major spatial numbering:\n\nROW 1\n1 = Coda\n2 = Chiave\n3 = Vittorio\n\nROW 2\n4 = Nico\n5 = VoiceBridge\n6 = Luce\n\nROW 3\n7 = Talon\n8 = Keel\n9 = Falcon\n\nThese numbers must remain stable unless Don explicitly changes the board layout.\n\nDo not dynamically renumber based on process state, model, availability, launch order, or runtime PID.\n\n────────────────────────────\nUI\n────────────────────────────\n\nDisplay the number clearly but unobtrusively on every tile.\n\nExamples:\n\n[1] Coda\n[2] Chiave\n[3] Vittorio\n\nor a small numeric badge.\n\nDo not replace the seat name with the number.\n\nDon needs to see BOTH:\n\nnumeric address + seat identity\n\n────────────────────────────\nCONFIG / DATA MODEL\n────────────────────────────\n\nPrefer adding an explicit stable field to the existing pane/seat configuration, e.g.:\n\ntileId: 1\nvoiceAlias: \"1\"\n\nUse the existing config architecture if equivalent fields already exist.\n\nDo not infer tile number from array order at runtime if an explicit stable identifier can be stored cleanly.\n\nRequired mapping:\n\n1 Coda\n2 Chiave\n3 Vittorio\n4 Nico\n5 VoiceBridge\n6 Luce\n7 Talon\n8 Keel\n9 Falcon\n\n────────────────────────────\nVOICEBRIDGE INTEGRATION\n────────────────────────────\n\nInspect the existing VoiceBridge command/control path.\n\nAdd or prepare the smallest mapping layer necessary so the following resolve to the corresponding DevPad tile:\n\n\"number one\" / \"number 1\" / \"one\" -> tile 1\n\"number two\" / \"number 2\" / \"two\" -> tile 2\n\nContinue through 9.\n\nAt minimum support explicit constructions:\n\n\"number N\"\n\"focus number N\"\n\"open number N\"\n\nIf bare-number recognition such as simply \"three\" could conflict with normal dictation, DO NOT enable it globally without a clear command context.\n\nPrefer deterministic phrases over aggressive voice interception.\n\n────────────────────────────\nACTION SEMANTICS\n────────────────────────────\n\nFor this pass, the primary action is:\n\nFOCUS / ACTIVATE THE EXISTING TILE\n\nDo not create duplicate sessions merely because Don says a number.\n\nIf the tile is already running:\n- focus/activate it\n\nIf the tile exists but its runtime is not started:\n- follow the existing DevPad behavior\n- do not invent new lifecycle semantics\n\nIf integration with OS/browser focus is not yet available:\n- implement the stable IDs and UI now\n- expose the numeric target through the existing DevPad control API\n- report the remaining VoiceBridge hook separately\n\n────────────────────────────\nIMPORTANT\n────────────────────────────\n\nNumber is a navigation address only.\n\nFor example:\n\n3 = Vittorio\n\nThat remains true whether Vittorio is currently running Kimi, another approved model, or is offline.\n\nNever allow:\n\nmodel -> number\nPID -> number\nlaunch order -> number\n\nThe board position / Don-approved config owns the number.\n\n────────────────────────────\nVERIFY\n────────────────────────────\n\nVerify all nine:\n\n1 -> Coda\n2 -> Chiave\n3 -> Vittorio\n4 -> Nico\n5 -> VoiceBridge\n6 -> Luce\n7 -> Talon\n8 -> Keel\n9 -> Falcon\n\nVerify:\n\n- numbers visible in UI\n- numbering survives DevPad restart\n- numbering does not change when a runtime restarts\n- inventory still works\n- seat labels remain intact\n- model/runtime identity remains separate\n- VoiceBridge can resolve at least \"number N\" to the correct tile/control target\n\n────────────────────────────\nRETURN\n────────────────────────────\n\nRESULT: PASS / PARTIAL / BLOCKED\n\nFILES CHANGED:\nExact files and purpose.\n\nNUMBER MAP:\nReturn 1 through 9.\n\nVOICEBRIDGE:\nState which spoken forms are supported.\n\nVERIFICATION:\nActual commands/tests performed.\n\nFINAL VERDICT:\nDEVPAD NUMERIC VOICE ADDRESSING READY\nor\nDEVPAD NUMERIC IDS READY — VOICE HOOK REMAINS\n```\n\nThis is worth doing **now**, because the 3×3 layout gives us a beautifully simple mental model: **1–3 top, 4–6 middle, 7–9 bottom**. Once you memorize that, VoiceBridge becomes much faster than saying seat names."]}, "create_time": 1790226908.87508, "end_turn": true, "id": "e953623e-37b3-446e-98f6-7eb7f879131b", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "lyiul9", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}}, "content_references": [], "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finish_details": {"stop_tokens": [200002], "type": "stop"}, "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab41b7c2620819187c626358eeb8a48", "is_complete": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "3fca5f0e-63df-44c0-aea8-96c948a201d9", "request_id": "c38cbe77-9990-491b-af0c-19aff8450635", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "search_result_groups": [], "story_events": [], "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "5881e386-8b09-4dd8-ac85-f472754afb21", "working_turn_id": "5881e386-8b09-4dd8-ac85-f472754afb21"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790226937.192564, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "