titute fields.\n\n==================================================\n7. STORE RESIDUE DEFINITION\n==================================================\n\nBased on evidence, answer:\n\nWhat does myDon need to persist itself, if anything?\n\nReturn the minimal set only.\n\nExamples:\n\nNONE\n\nor\n\nrouting-audit.json:\n- handoffId\n- routedBy\n- routedAt\n- targetSeat\n- deliveryResult\n\nor\n\nminimal fallback:\n- handoffId\n- lifecycle state\n- route intent\n- delivery outcome\n\nDo not propose:\n- monthly logs\n- snapshots\n- compaction\n- projections\nunless current system genuinely requires them.\n\n==================================================\n8. INBOX ROUTING MECHANIC\n==================================================\n\nState the cleanest ACTUAL route operation supported by current implementation:\n\nOne of:\n\nASSIGN EXISTING ITEM TO SEAT\n\nMOVE EXISTING ITEM TO SEAT INBOX\n\nCOPY ITEM TO TARGET INBOX WITH SAME DETERMINISTIC ID\n\nWRITE NEW TARGET INBOX ITEM\n\nUNSUPPORTED WITHOUT NEW LOGIC\n\nExplain exact function/API/file mechanism.\n\nThis is critical for Nico's future implementation brief.\n\n==================================================\n9. IDEMPOTENCY / FAILURE REALITY CHECK\n==================================================\n\nTest or inspect enough to determine:\n\n- Can same item be routed twice to same seat without duplicate?\n- Can a duplicate be detected by ID?\n- Can failed writes be observed?\n- Can retry be explicit?\n- Can route intent survive a restart?\n- Can target inbox be checked for existing item by ID?\n\nDo not perform destructive testing.\n\nIf a safe test requires writes:\nSTOP and report what would need to be tested later.\n\nClassify each:\n\nPROVEN\nSUPPORTED BY CODE BUT NOT TESTED\nNOT SUPPORTED\nUNKNOWN\n\n==================================================\n10. DO-NOT-TOUCH BOUNDARY\n==================================================\n\nDuring this recon:\n\nDo not:\n- write new inbox items unless explicitly necessary and safely non-destructive\n- modify queue files\n- edit server code\n- add myDon files\n- create data/mydon\n- change schemas\n- refactor MCP\n- alter seat registry\n- change DevPad grid\n- change runtime/model bindings\n- touch VoiceBridge\n- change permissions\n- rotate credentials\n- kill processes\n- restart DevPad unless absolutely required for read-only verification\n\nThis is reconnaissance only.\n\n==================================================\n11. REQUIRED RETURN FORMAT\n==================================================\n\nReturn exactly these sections.\n\n## 1. EXECUTIVE GROUND TRUTH\n\nMaximum 12 lines.\n\nState:\n- what the current inbox actually is\n- whether it can serve as myDon's queue\n- whether routing is assign/move/copy/write\n- whether stable IDs exist\n- whether myDon needs its own store\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n## 2. CURRENT INBOX ESTATE\n\nPaths, modules, APIs, files, processes.\n\nIdentify current implementation truth versus stale/supporting material.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n## 3. R1–R8 FINDINGS\n\nAnswer each recon question separately.\n\nUse:\nSUPPORTED\nPARTIAL\nNOT SUPPORTED\nUNKNOWN\n\nwith evidence.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n## 4. BRANCH DECISION\n\nA / B / C\n\nExplain why in no more than 10 lines.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n## 5. FIELD MAPPING TABLE\n\nDesired myDon field\n→ current inbox representation\n→ support level\n→ mutation capability\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n## 6. ROUTING MECHANIC\n\nState exactly how route should work using CURRENT capabilities.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n## 7. MINIMUM myDon RESIDUE\n\nState the exact smallest extra persistence required.\n\nIf none:\nsay NONE.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n## 8. IDEMPOTENCY / FAILURE SUPPORT\n\nStable IDs\nduplicate guard\nretry\ndelivery errors\nrestart recovery\nlookup-by-ID\n\nClassify each.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n## 9. UI REFRESH MECHANISM\n\nPush / poll / manual / other.\n\nState what already exists.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n## 10. BLOCKERS / GAPS\n\nOnly real gaps that Nico will need to implement.\n\nDo not redesign.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n## 11. NICO IMPLEMENTATION INPUT\n\nReturn a short mechanical summary:\n\n- branch\n- canonical queue source\n- route operation\n- IDs\n- statuses\n- query method\n- audit location\n- required new state, if any\n- exact existing modules Nico should reuse\n\nThis section should be usable directly in the future Nico build prompt.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n## 12. FINAL LUCE VERDICT\n\nChoose one:\n\nINBOX READY FOR myDon — NO NEW QUEUE REQUIRED\n\nINBOX READY FOR myDon — SMALL HOLDING LANE REQUIRED\n\nINBOX PARTIAL — MINIMAL myDon FALLBACK STATE REQUIRED\n\nGROUND NOT YET ESTABLISHED\n\nThen provide no more than 5 next actions.\n\n==================================================\n12. GOVERNING PRINCIPLE\n==================================================\n\nThe desired outcome is NOT:\n\n\"Design a better inbox.\"\n\nThe desired outcome is:\n\n\"Tell Don exactly what the current inbox already supports so myDon can reuse it with the smallest possible new machinery.\"\n\nPreferred architecture if evidence allows:\n\nexisting inbox\n→ Don reviews through /mydon\n→ Don routes by stable seat identity\n→ target inbox receives the same deterministic handoff\n→ myDon records only what the inbox cannot\n→ later phases add DevPad focus, ping, VoiceBridge\n\nKeep this pass read-only, evidence-first, and brutally narrow.\n```\n\nThat should give Luce exactly the right assignment: **ground the inbox first, then let Nico build mechanically from the evidence instead of guessing the queue architecture.**"]}, "create_time": 1790229194.705933, "end_turn": true,