orks**. Seats launch into the proper `GCE_IDENTITY\\<Seat>` homes and load their identities automatically.\n\nCurrent primary 3×3 board:\n\n```text\n┌────────────┬────────────┬────────────┐\n│ 1 Coda     │ 2 Chiave   │ 3 Vittorio │\n├────────────┼────────────┼────────────┤\n│ 4 Nico     │ 5 Voice    │ 6 Luce     │\n├────────────┼────────────┼────────────┤\n│ 7 Talon    │ 8 Keel     │ 9 Falcon   │\n└────────────┴────────────┴────────────┘\n```\n\nBinding doctrine remains:\n\n```text\nTILE != SEAT != MODEL != RUNTIME != PROVIDER\nMODEL != SEAT\n```\n\nThe numeric addresses are stable navigation aliases for VoiceBridge and Don muscle memory.\n\n### Current Coda posture\n\nWe stopped making **embedded ChatGPT inside the DevPad** a requirement.\n\nCoda can remain an external managed ChatGPT/browser surface for now. That is acceptable because the real operational problem is **not where Coda renders**.\n\nThe real problem is:\n\n> **Don should not be manually copying Coda's work into another terminal.**\n\nThat becomes the next architecture problem.\n\n---\n\n# 2. Current DevPad future visual extension\n\nAfter the primary 3×3 is stable, Don wants to see one additional utility row and judge the density visually:\n\n```text\n┌────────────┬────────────┬────────────┐\n│ Coda       │ Chiave     │ Vittorio   │\n├────────────┼────────────┼────────────┤\n│ Nico       │ Voice      │ Luce       │\n├────────────┼────────────┼────────────┤\n│ Talon      │ Keel       │ Falcon     │\n├────────────┼────────────┼────────────┤\n│ Bedrock    │ OPEN/TBD   │ Kimi AdHoc │\n└────────────┴────────────┴────────────┘\n```\n\nThe bottom row is **utility/runtime space**, not additional stable seats.\n\nKnown candidates:\n\n- **Bedrock Mantle**\n- **open/TBD**\n- **Kimi ad hoc**\n\nNo further layout commitment until Don actually sees the density.\n\nLikely later UX improvement:\n\n**condensed VS Code-style shell** with a lightweight quick-access rail/banner/footer for important GCE roots and project