kely strongest eventual architecture:\n\n```text\nEMAIL / lightweight envelope\n        +\nDrive/local filesystem / heavy artifact\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nHDO-0041\nFROM: Coda\nTO: Nico\nPROJECT: DevPad\n\nObjective:\nFix runtime binding.\n\nPAYLOAD:\nDrive/path reference to detailed artifact\n```\n\nEmail moves the instruction/envelope.\n\nLarge reports, architecture specs, logs, patches, etc. remain as referenced artifacts.\n\n---\n\n# 11. Standard Pigeon envelope\n\nWhatever transport wins, Coda should emit structured handoffs rather than arbitrary copy/paste blobs.\n\nWorking envelope:\n\n```text\nHANDOFF_ID: HDO-<deterministic-id>\nFROM_SEAT: Coda\nTO_SEAT: Nico\nPROJECT: GCE_DevPad_Command_Center\nTYPE: IMPLEMENTATION\nPRIORITY: NORMAL\nSTATUS: READY_TO_ROUTE\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n...\n\nCONTEXT:\n...\n\nINSTRUCTIONS:\n...\n\nARTIFACTS:\n...\n\nSTOP_CONDITIONS:\n...\n\nRETURN_TO:\nCoda / Don\n```\n\nReturn traffic keeps the same `HANDOFF_ID`.\n\nThat gives us deterministic correlation:\n\n```text\nHDO-0041 outbound\nHDO-0041 return\n```\n\n---\n\n# 12. End-state operating flow\n\nThis is the target.\n\n```text\n                         DON\n                          │\n                    talks / clicks\n                          │\n                 ┌────────▼────────┐\n                 │      CODA       │\n                 │ ChatGPT / other │\n                 │ approved runtime│\n                 └────────┬────────┘\n                          │\n                  structured handoff\n                          │\n                 ┌────────▼────────┐\n                 │    CABLE CAR    │\n                 │ transport path  │\n                 └────────┬────────┘\n                          │\n                 ┌────────▼────────┐\n                 │     PIGEON      │\n                 │ courier/confirm │\n                 └────────┬────────┘\n                          │\n                      _shared\n                          │\n                 ┌────────▼────────┐\n                 │     myDon       │\n                 │ orchestration   │\n                 └────────┬────────┘\n                          │\n                     Don routes\n                          │\n              ┌───────────▼────────────┐\n              │ Main DevPad / Command  │\n              │ Center seat estate     │\n              └───────────┬────────────┘\n                          │\n                  Nico/Luce/etc.\n                          │\n                    return handoff\n                          │\n                 Pigeon/Cable Car\n                          │\n                     Coda + Don\n```\n\nThat is the system we are actually building.\n\n---\n\n# 13. Explicitly **not** building\n\nDo not accidentally turn this into:\n\n- autonomous agent-to-agent government\n- another seat registry\n- another queue database\n- OpenRouter as infrastructure\n- OpenCode as universal transport\n- Bedrock as routing authority\n- Google Drive as seat authority\n- email as seat authority\n- PID-based routing\n- model-based routing\n- another giant framework rewrite\n\nBedrock, OpenAI, Kimi, GLM, etc. are **compute/runtime options**.\n\nThey are not the routing layer.\n\n---\n\n# 14. Next-session starting order\n\nWhen we resume:\n\n**1. Verify/freeze current DevPad.**  \nNo more uncontrolled changes while we start another surface.\n\n**2. Convert Luce's inbox recon into the Nico Phase-1 myDon implementation brief.**\n\n**3. Build only `/mydon` queue → click target → move-with-ID → next.**\n\n**4. Luce verifies the eight routing invariants.**\n\n**5. Add in-DevPad focus.**\n\n**6. Separately pressure-test Cable Car transports:**\nGoogle Drive vs dedicated email/Proton Bridge vs hybrid.\n\n**7. Define Pigeon's two-way transport contract.**\n\n**8. Connect external Coda to that lane.**\n\nAt that point, **where Coda physically renders stops mattering**.\n\nThe milestone we are chasing is not “Coda is embedded.”\n\nIt is:\n\n> **Don speaks to Coda once, and work moves through GCE without Don copying another fucking prompt.**\n\n**ANCHOR STATUS: FROZEN FOR NEXT SESSION.**"]}, "create_time": 1790229787.823581, "end_turn": true, "id": "cd54813e-18e7-48d8-8746-c9b9d516fb33", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "ydn9oq", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "1": {"edited": false, "id": "6ag3rj", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "10": {"edited": false, "id": "3zldsz", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "11": {"edited": false, "id": "lsp493", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "12": {"edited": false, "id": "iujneb", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "13": {"edited": false, "id": "irv7qg", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "14": {"edited": false, "id": "z3t2ft", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "15": {"edited": false, "id": "4lz000", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "16": {"edited": false, "id": "rvhvkf", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "17": {"edited": false, "id": "k8b4q0", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "18": {"edited": false, "id": "6stbrp", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "19": {"edited": false, "id": "1vo5jq", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "2": {"edited": false, "id": "hrsdg6", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "20": {"edited": false, "id": "uqosih", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "21": {"edited": false, "id": "qg1ptb", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "22": {"edited": false, "id": "tjinoo", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "23": {"edited": false, "id": "amylrq", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "24": {"edited": false, "id": "vyyol9", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "25": {"edited": false, "id": "5qxzk0", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "26": {"edited": false, "id