lt_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finished_duration_sec": 11, "hide_inline_actions": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "ce43b38c-62d1-424a-9580-ac5da46a5b64", "reasoning_end_time": 1790261533.967409, "reasoning_recap_type": "hide_all", "reasoning_start_time": 1790261522.0645194, "reasoning_status": "reasoning_ended", "request_id": "7466f4b9-5660-494c-8226-41ebc8aef0e7", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "fbda75ec-732f-429a-8620-e1f9f9f49f28", "working_turn_id": "fbda75ec-732f-429a-8620-e1f9f9f49f28"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790261534.06643, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["**STATUS: PROVISIONAL ROOKIE DEPTH CHART · Confidence 95%**\n\nYep. Now that we have the **Main DevPad roles** and the current **free OpenCode bench**, I would build Rookie as a **role substitution board**, not a universal “best model” board.\n\nThe Black Pearl already told us that model labor is specialized: Nex Pro was strongest at grounded restraint, Muse 1.3 at disciplined pattern work, Dots at anomalies, Big Pickle at verification, while Qwen was only a retrieval candidate and never got a fair Trial 01 because of rate limits. fileciteturn3file0\n\n## Main → Rookie substitution map\n\n| Main seat | Main job | Rookie free substitute | Why |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **1 Coda** | Strategic advisor / governance / reconciliation | **Nex N2.5 Pro Free** | Best grounded restraint of the free Black Pearl bench. Excellent evidence-vs-claim discipline and low storytelling. Closest free option for bounded Coda-style reasoning. |\n| **2 Chiave** | Architecture / integration | **Nex N2.5 Pro Free** *provisional* | There is **no validated free GLM-5.1-equivalent architect** in the current pool. Nex Pro is the safest substitute because it will stop where evidence stops instead of inventing architecture. |\n| **3 Vittorio** | Technical advisor / challenge / warboard | **Dots3 Note Preview Free** | Strongest validated free anomaly hunter. Good at finding the weird thing everybody else missed and challenging the prevailing read. |\n| **4 Nico** | Implementation hammer / builder | **MiMo-V2.6-Flash Free** *field trial* | Not validated by the old Black Pearl trial—the artifact tested MiMo V2, not 2.6—but **our current operational experience is materially better with 2.6 Flash**. This is exactly what Rookie should pressure-test. |\n| **5 VoiceBridge** | Voice/service lane | **No model substitution** | VoiceBridge is infrastructure, not a cognitive seat. Rookie should point to the same service or an isolated test instance—not assign an LLM just to fill the square. |\n| **6 Luce** | Verification / ground truth | **Big Pickle** if promo-free remains available; otherwise **Nex N2.5 Mini Free** | Big Pickle already earned the verification/truth-checking berth. Nex Mini is the best current fallback: excellent missing-data restraint and low storytelling. |\n| **7 Talon** | Operations / sequencing / routing | **Muse Spark 1.3 Free** | Clean, disciplined, restrained. Strong cross-workstream pattern recognition without trying to become the architect. Very good fit for “what happens next?” |\n| **8 Keel** | Build/deploy / operational execution | **MiMo-V2.6-Flash Free** *provisional* | Same reason as Nico, but with a tighter bounded deployment brief. We need a fresh code/build trial before promoting this as proven. |\n| **9 Falcon** | Data acquisition / retrieval | **Qwen3.8 27B Free** | The Black Pearl labor map specifically left Qwen in the **gathering/retrieval candidate** lane. The earlier trial was rate-limited rather than a model-quality failure. This is exactly where I would retest it. |\n\n### Rookie board I would actually boot\n\n```text\n┌────────────────────┬────────────────────┬────────────────────┐\n│ 1 CODA             │ 2 CHIAVE           │ 3 VITTORIO         │\n│ Nex N2.5 Pro       │ Nex N2.5 Pro       │ Dots3 Note Preview │\n├────────────────────┼────────────────────┼────────────────────┤\n│ 4 NICO             │ 5 VOICEBRIDGE      │ 6 LUCE             │\n│ MiMo V2.6 Flash    │ Service            │ Big Pickle*        │\n│                    │                    │ Nex Mini fallback  │\n├────────────────────┼────────────────────┼────────────────────┤\n│ 7 TALON            │ 8 KEEL             │ 9 FALCON           │\n│ Muse Spark 1.3     │ MiMo V2.6 Flash    │ Qwen3.8 27B       │\n└────────────────────┴────────────────────┴────────────────────┘\n```\n\n`*` assuming the Big Pickle free/promo route is still live when Rookie launches.\n\n## The interesting part: duplicates are fine\n\nI **wouldn't force nine different models** just to make Rookie look diverse.\n\nIf Nex Pro is our strongest free grounded brain, then having it occupy both **Coda and provisional Chiave** is completely consistent with:\n\n> **MODEL != SEAT**\n\nSame model, different bootstrap, different seat authority, different job.\n\nLikewise MiMo can occupy **Nico + Keel** while we're testing whether V2.6 Flash is actually a dependable implementation family.\n\nThat itself becomes useful research: *does the same runtime behave differently when loaded into Nico vs Keel doctrine?*\n\n## Where I would *not* waste Rookie slots\n\nBased on Black Pearl evidence:\n\n**Nemotron 3.5 Lightning** — prior ~10-minute latency plus missing-game/data errors. Not worth a persistent seat.\n\n**Nemotron 3 Ultra** — too much gap filling / speculation for trusted work.\n\n**Laguna XS 2.1** — major logic/data errors. We already saw enough.\n\n**LFM2.5-2.6B** — maybe someday for dirt-cheap routing/classification, but not a working seat.\n\n**North Mini Code** — interesting name for Nico, but our actual trial failed provenance/artifact expectations. I wouldn't promote it because it says “Code.”\n\n**Inkling** — needs a clean identity test before we know what we actually have.\n\n### Two rookies I *do* want on the bench\n\n**Muse Spark 1.2** = first reserve.  \nIt wasn't as clean as 1.3, but it performed well enough to earn a second-interview/reserve designation.\n\n**Ling 3.0 Flash Fin** = specialist reserve.  \nNot trusted for primary grounded work, but its market-structure curiosity was interesting enough to keep around for deliberately bounded challenge work. fileciteturn3file0\n\nSo I'd define Rookie as **9 active slots + bench**, not “nine free models and we're done.”\n\nAnd the biggest unresolved slot is **Chiave**. We have no free model that has demonstrated the architectural/integration behavior GLM 5.1 demonstrated. I would deliberately mark Rookie Chiave:\n\n> **NEX PRO — ACTING / PROVISIONAL**\n\nrather than pretending we solved that substitution. memcite"]}, "create_time": 1790261534.084784, "end_turn": true, "id": "7691e3b7-5792-4e07-ad36-9ebf078ebcd7", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [{"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 554, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "files/search", "authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "b873454e-620b-452f-93ad-4460dcb65c6b", "cited_message_idx": 421, "cloud_doc_url": "", "connector_id": null, "doi": null, "effective_time": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "library_artifact_type": "sheet", "library_file_id": "libfile_d695fbccf7b881918f38fa61d59528ca", "line_range": null, "publication_year": null, "retrieval_file_index": 0, "retrieval_turn": 3, "run_id": null, "search_result_idx": null, "set_id": null, "source_icon_url": null, "source_label": null, "source_url": null, "spl_version": null, "title": null}, "id": "file_00000000871081fdb71e83538754ca64", "name": "BLACK_PEARL_MODEL_LAB_AND_EC_ANCHOR_2026-09-18.xlsx", "source": "my_files", "text": "", "type": "file"}, "start_ix": 533}, {"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 5541, "metadata": 