lection()` && `getSelection()` non-empty; **empty fires are ignored** (this is the deliberate workaround for your destructive mousemove) |\n[L36] | 4 | capture-phase `mousedown`: `button !== 2` → clears **both** `rightSnap` and `lastSelection` (intent moved away); `button === 2` → press snapshot (unchanged) |\n[L37] | 5 | `contextmenu` priority: **press snapshot (fresh) → early cache (fresh) → live selection (legacy fallback)**; on copy → `lastSelection = null` (one-shot consume) |\n[L38] | 6 | `copySelection()` (Ctrl+Shift+C path) → consumes the cache too |\n\n[L40] **TTL rationale (from YOUR harness, not a guess):** `gate7c` variants B/C run\n[L41] `selectRow → sleep(350) → mousemove → sleep(120) → selProbe → rightClick (move + sleep(80) + press)`\n[L42] → drag-end to contextmenu ≈ **700–1100 ms**. TTL must clear that with margin. Your stale-safety\n[L43] (L197-211) and cross-tile leak (L228-241) checks are **invalidation-based (left click), not\n[L44] time-based** — `clearSelection()`/`clearComposer()` both land a left `mousedown` inside `.term`,\n[L45] which my handler uses to null the cache — so TTL = 5000 ms does not and cannot weaken them.\n\n[L47] ## 3. CACHE LIFECYCLE\n\n[L49] - **SET/REFRESH** — `onSelectionChange` fires with non-empty selection → overwrite (new selection replaces old).\n[L50] - **INVALIDATE** — any non-right `mousedown` inside the tile's `.term` element (covers your `clearSelection`, `clearComposer`, center-click, and the left-press at drag start).\n[L51] - **CONSUME (one-shot)** — right-click copy path and Ctrl+Shift+C copy path both null it.\n[L52] - **EXPIRE** — `Date.now() - at >= 5000` at contextmenu → treated as absent (falls through to paste).\n[L53] - **NEVER cleared** by the empty-selection fire the destructive mousemove produces.\n\n[L55] ## 4. STATIC VALIDATION (run)\n\n[L57] - `node --check public\\renderer.js` → **PASS (exit 0)**\n[L58] - Structural assertions **14/14 PASS**: both D-1 `ev.preventDefault()` present · `onSelect