se mousemove listener**, which finally intercepts the selection before xterm destroys it.\n\n8. Every one of those small changes was wrapped in the full process:\n   **Nico builds → handoff → Luce reloads/tests → evidence matrix → failure report → new handoff → Nico reopens → probes → patches → validates → routes back.**\n\nThat’s where the day disappeared.\n\nSo the real diagnosis is:\n\n> **We treated a non-critical right-click convenience behavior like a release-blocking systems defect.**\n\nThe copy/paste bug did **not** deserve nine hours. The process did this:\n\n**tiny defect → forensic isolation → independent verification → new hypothesis → another implementation → another verification → runtime instrumentation → another implementation → another gate**\n\nAnd I made it worse by continuing to recommend another bounded pass every time instead of saying much earlier:\n\n> Ctrl+Shift+C works. Ctrl+Shift+V works. Ship the DevPad and defer right-click copy.\n\nThat should have happened after D-1 went green.\n\n### What was worth the time\n\nA few things were genuinely learned:\n\n- duplicate paste was real and is fixed\n- xterm’s selection lifecycle is weird\n- right-mousedown was too late\n- `onSelectionChange` did not behave the way the static model suggested\n- capture-phase mouse handling is the correct place if you insist on custom right-click copy\n\nBut none of that justifies holding the whole DevPad hostage.\n\n### What should happen now\n\n**No more architecture. No more handoff loop. No more “final certification matrix.”**\n\nLoad the current renderer, verify the board itself works, and use:\n\n- `Ctrl+Shift+C` = copy\n- `Ctrl+Shift+V` = paste\n- `Shift+Insert` = paste\n- `Ctrl+C` = interrupt\n\nIf right-click copy works now, great. If it does not, **defer it**.\n\nThat is what should have happened hours ago."]}, "create_time": 1790314379.95063, "end_turn": true, "id": "ae1cc6b3-18fc-461d-9535-538ed7263eee", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": []