ew MiniMax-family model — someone found tokenizer behavior consistent with MiniMax — but that is *not confirmed*. citeturn151463reddit46turn151463search8\nAlso, don't interpret “free sub-agents” as unlimited infrastructure. OpenCode has some current free-tier quirks around which sub-agent types can run and under what session context; there are active issues around free-tier subagent behavior. citeturn151463search4turn151463search6\nSo for **your** stack, I wouldn't replace Big Pickle yet. I'd give Space Bunny a very specific job:\n> **Carousel candidate / orchestration stress-test model.**\nRun the *exact same mature MLB or Voice Bridge lane* through Big Pickle and Space Bunny: same session header, same bootstrap transitions, same stop gates. Measure **role adherence, unauthorized decisions, number of interventions, context retention across bootstrap swaps, sub-agent discipline, and wall-clock time.**\nThat will tell us a hell of a lot more than a generic benchmark. Because what you care about isn't “is Space Bunny smart?” It's **“can Space Bunny drive the GCE role carousel without Don babysitting it?”**\nAnd based on what I'm seeing, **that's absolutely worth testing.** memcite\n", "start_idx": 0, "title": "New chat", "type": "grouped_webpages", "url": "https://chatgpt.com/c/6ab5eed8-32c0-83e8-80dc-91952f50c81e"}, "citation_uuid": "aab447d4-47a3-4934-bc86-58995422ab7c", "deleted": false, "feedback": null, "retrieval_origin": "pca"}], "conversation_context_citation_metadata_status": "seeded", "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": false, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "disable_turn_actions": true, "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab41b7c2620819187c626358eeb8a48", "hide_inline_actions": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "f56ce010-ed64-4730-bde7-0eadf72aa09e", "permissions": [{"notification_channel_id": "thinking", "notification_channel_name": "Thinking", "notificat