ins:\n\n**Vittorio advises. Chiave architects. Nico builds. Corrado computes.**\n\nAnd:\n\n**IDENTITY != ROLE != LENS != PERSONALITY != AUTHORITY != MODEL**  \n**MODEL != SEAT**\n\n## Blackhole-loop anchor\n\nThe failure we are exiting is now clear:\n\n> A bounded maintenance request — fix DevPad copy/paste and make a small Seat 1 change — lost its global frame. A legitimate verification finding repeatedly became a new implementation slice. Coda kept authorizing “one more bounded pass,” Nico kept building locally reasonable fixes, Luce kept correctly disproving assumptions, and the session stopped producing visible outcomes for Don.\n\nThe critical distinction is:\n\n**Luce finding a defect was not the loop.**  \n**Coda converting every finding into another mandatory build/certification cycle was the loop.**\n\nThe second critical distinction:\n\n**The seats mostly remained disciplined locally. The session became undisciplined globally.**\n\n## Recovery controls now active\n\nFrom this point forward in this recon:\n\n- no continuing the DevPad build\n- no clipboard fixes\n- no Rookie build\n- no myDon build\n- no architecture invention\n- no new slices\n- no new certification gates\n- no Drive changes\n- no turning postmortem findings into implementation work\n- no treating planned/spec’d work as built\n- no treating static validation as visible product success\n\nWe preserve the original bounded ask and reconstruct only what happened.\n\nThe control sequence we are restoring is:\n\n**CLEAR ASK → one coherent pass → visible runnable artifact → bounded verification → bounded fix only if core outcome fails → final verification → CLOSE**\n\nNot:\n\n**finding → slice → verifier → reframe → slice → verifier → reframe**\n\n## Circuit-breaker doctrine restored\n\nThe first circuit breaker should fire when any of these appear:\n\n- repeated “one more slice”\n- repeated verification without a new runnable artifact\n- architectural reasoning appearing inside a maintenance task\n- verifier findings repeatedly creating implementation work\n- Don can no longer point to visible progress\n- session header/footer disappears or stops governing the work\n- settled premises start getting reopened across multiple seats\n- confidence/reporting grows while the actual usable outcome does not\n\nA verified artifact should normally trigger **closure or an explicitly authorized new phase**, not automatic recursive work.\n\n## Session footer format restored\n\nEvery meaningful checkpoint from here should close with:\n\n**STATUS:** PROCEED / CHECKPOINT / STOP  \n**CONFIDENCE:** percentage + brief rationale  \n**OUTCOME:** what was actually established  \n**ARTIFACTS:** actual artifacts only  \n**KEY DECISIONS:** accepted decisions only  \n**OPEN ITEMS:** unresolved items + owner  \n**NEXT ROUTE:** one route only  \n**DON INPUT NEEDED:** YES / NO  \n**ANCHOR STATUS:** updated / unchanged\n\nFor this recovery session, the current footer is:\n\n**STATUS:** CHECKPOINT  \n**CONFIDENCE:** 99% — loop mechanism and session frame failure are now materially established from the thread  \n**OUTCOME:** Framework session shell restored; blackhole loop isolated as orchestration/frame failure rather than primarily a model-quality failure  \n**ARTIFACTS:** 10-hour DevPad postmortem already reconstructed in this chat  \n**KEY DECISIONS:** no build, no repair, no certification while in recon; preserve original ask; distinguish designed / implemented / verified / visible  \n**OPEN ITEMS:** reconcile this session against the other contaminated chats and extract durable framework lessons without reopening implementation  \n**NEXT ROUTE:** Don + Coda cross-session reconciliation  \n**DON INPUT NEEDED:** NO for grounding  \n**ANCHOR STATUS:** ACTIVE — blackhole-loop recovery frame restored\n\nWe’re back inside the framework now. No more drifting. memcite"]}, "create_time": 1790364203.943759, "end_turn": true, "id": "7cae05c8-1d72-4b03-9166-78dc4639a582", "metadata": {"can_sa