anchor status\n- whether a persistent session frame existed\n- where frame discipline disappeared\n\nE. VISIBLE PRODUCT STATE\n- what Don could actually see/use at meaningful checkpoints\n- whether a new visible artifact existed after each major pass\n\nF. PROJECT / CONTEXT BLEED\n- identify only causal bleed\n- do not call normal context \"contamination\" without evidence\n\nEach sub-recon must remain READ ONLY.\n\nDo not create implementation recommendations.\n\n==================================================\nREQUIRED EVENT TIMELINE\n==================================================\n\nBuild a chronological timeline beginning from the first real maintenance request.\n\nFor EVERY significant event, capture:\n\nTIME / ORDER:\nSEAT:\nACTION:\nCLAIM:\nEVIDENCE:\nARTIFACT:\nVISIBLE TO DON? YES / NO\nSTATE CLASS:\n- VERIFIED\n- SUPPORTED\n- ASSUMED\n- UNKNOWN\n- DISPROVED\n\nInclude at minimum:\n\n- original copy/paste request\n- Seat 1 change\n- initial clipboard diagnosis\n- D-1 duplicate paste\n- first D-2 theory\n- first Luce failure\n- mousedown snapshot fix\n- Luce mousemove finding\n- onSelectionChange theory\n- Nico implementation\n- Luce proof cache was inert\n- runtime probe\n- capture-phase mousemove implementation\n- final state reached\n- any point where Rookie DevPad or other functionality was discussed as \"next\"\n\n==================================================\nASSUMPTION LEDGER\n==================================================\n\nCreate an explicit ledger:\n\nASSUMPTION\nWHO INTRODUCED IT\nWHY IT WAS BELIEVED\nWAS IT VERIFIED BEFORE BUILD?\nWHAT HAPPENED?\nFINAL STATUS\n\nSpecial attention:\n\n- selection survives until right-mousedown\n- right-button press destroys selection\n- mousemove destroys selection\n- onSelectionChange is early enough\n- static simulation represents live browser path\n- right-click copy is a release blocker\n- clipboard had to be fully certified before other DevPad work\n- Rookie DevPad was being built\n- optimization work was underway\n\nDo not assign blame without evidence.\n\n==================================================\nSLICE / GATE LEDGER\n==================================================\n\nEnumerate every meaningful slice or gate.\n\nFor each:\n\nSLICE ID / DESCRIPTION:\nCREATED BY:\nWHY CREATED:\nINPUT:\nOUTPUT:\nACTUAL CODE/ARTIFACT PRODUCED:\nVISIBLE PRODUCT CHANGE:\nNECESSARY?\nCOULD HAVE BEEN ABSORBED INTO PRIOR PASS?\nDID IT CREATE ANOTHER SLICE?\nFINAL VALUE:\n\nThis is critical.\n\nWe need to know how a small maintenance task became a 10-hour chain.\n\n==================================================\nSEAT BEHAVIOR AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nEvaluate each seat separately.\n\nCODA:\n- Was framing preserved?\n- Did Coda keep the original objective visible?\n- Did Coda infer architecture?\n- Did Coda convert verifier findings into new mandatory slices?\n- Did Coda lose proportionality between severity and effort?\n- Did Coda call something \"next\" that was not being built?\n\nNICO:\n- Did Nico implement exactly what was asked?\n- Did Nico introduce unverified implementation assumptions?\n- Did Nico distinguish static proof from behavioral proof?\n- Was Nico repeatedly rebuilding the same local problem?\n\nLUCE:\n- Were findings legitimate?\n- Did Luce remain read/test/verify?\n- Did Luce propose design directions?\n- Did those suggestions become de facto architecture?\n- Did Luce repeatedly re-certify already-established state?\n\nCHIAVE:\n- Was Chiave invoked?\n- If not, should architecture ever have escalated there?\n- Do NOT invent an answer if architecture was never actually required.\n\nVITTORIO:\n- Was technical challenge/warboard used?\n- If absent, note absence only.\n- Do not claim it should have been used unless evidence supports that conclusion.\n\nDON:\n- What did Don actually request?\n- When did Don begin signaling dissatisfaction/loss of progress?\n- When did Don explicitly identify the loop?\n\n==================================================\nVISIBLE OUTCOME LEDGER\n==================================================\n\nAt every major checkpoint answer:\n\nWHAT COULD DON ACTUALLY SEE OR USE NOW THAT HE COULD NOT BEFORE?\n\nUse strict classifications:\n\nVISIBLE NEW FUNCTIONALITY\nVISIBLE MAINTENANCE IMPROVEMENT\nINTERNAL TECHNICAL CHANGE ONLY\nTEST / CERTIFICATION ONLY\nNO PRODUCT CHANGE\n\nIf nothing visible changed, say:\n\nNO NEW VISIBLE OUTCOME\n\nDo not count:\n- prompts\n- handoffs\n- tests\n- hashes\n- discussions\n- planned features\nas visible product functionality.\n\n==================================================\nFRAME HEALTH AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nDetermine:\n\n- Was there an initial session header?\n- Was there a durable session ID?\n- Was the expected artifact frozen?\n- Was scope frozen?\n- Was there a timebox?\n- Was there a retry ceiling?\n- Was there a severity classification?\n- Was there a stop condition?\n- Was there a visible outcome checkpoint?\n- Was there a session footer?\n- Did footers exist only at seat level?\n- Did local seat discipline survive while global session discipline failed?\n\nIdentify exact evidence.\n\n==================================================\nPROJECT / CONTEXT BLEED\n==================================================\n\nCheck whether:\n\n- Rookie DevPad discussion\n- myDon\n- Cable Car\n- Pigeon\n- resource optimization\n- model testing\n- broader GCE framework context\n\ncausally altered this maintenance task.\n\nClassify each:\n\nNO EFFECT\nEXPECTATION BLEED\nPROCESS BLEED\nTECHNICAL BLEED\nUNKNOWN\n\nDo not overstate.\n\n==================================================\nDELIVERABLE AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nStrictly classify each claimed result as:\n\nDESIGNED\nSPECIFIED\nIMPLEMENTED\nSTATICALLY VALIDATED\nBEHAVIORALLY VERIFIED\nVISIBLE TO DON\nCURRENTLY WORKING\nUNKNOWN\n\nDo not collapse these states.\n\n==================================================\nSALVAGE AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nClassify every meaningful artifact/findings:\n\nKEEP\nVERIFY\nDISCARD\nUNKNOWN\n\nExamples:\n\n- Seat 1 conversion\n- D-1 preventDefault fix\n- D-2 mousedown snapshot\n- onSelectionChange cache\n- capture-phase cache\n- test harnesses\n- handoffs\n- runtime findings\n- repeated certification artifacts\n\n==================================================\nROOT CAUSE\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT force one root cause.\n\nRank evidence for:\n\n- missing session framing\n- unclear stop condition\n- Coda orchestration drift\n- overslicing\n- verifier recursion\n- builder fragmentation\n- architecture guessed before runtime measurement\n- project/context overloading\n- handoff information loss\n- release-severity misclassification\n- loss of visible outcome discipline\n- another cause discovered from evidence\n\nUse:\n\nVERY STRONG\nSTRONG\nMODERATE\nWEAK\nNO EVIDENCE\n\n==================================================\nFINAL REQUIRED RETURN\n==================================================\n\nReturn one forensic report.\n\nNO FIXES.\nNO NEW ARCHITECTURE.\nNO IMPLEMENTATION PROMPTS.\n\nStructure:\n\n1. EXECUTIVE FINDING\n\n2. ORIGINAL ASK\n\n3. STARTING STATE\n\n4. EXPECTED WORK SIZE\n\n5. CHRONOLOGICAL TIMELINE\n\n6. ACTUAL CODE / FILE CHANGES\n\n7. ASSUMPTION LEDGER\n\n8. SLICE / GATE LEDGER\n\n9. SEAT BEHAVIOR AUDIT\n   - Don\n   - Coda\n   - Nico\n   - Luce\n   - other seats if materially involved\n\n10. VERIFICATION AUDIT\n\n11. VISIBLE OUTCOME LEDGER\n\n12. FRAME HEALTH\n\n13. PROJECT / CONTEXT BLEED\n\n14. DELIVERABLE STATE MATRIX\n\n15. SALVAGE\n   KEEP / VERIFY / DISCARD / UNKNOWN\n\n16. ROOT-CAUSE RANKING\n\n17. FIRST CIRCUIT BREAKER\n\n18. EARLY WARNING SIGNALS\n\n19. FINAL POSTMORTEM\n\nFINAL FOOTER:\n\nSESSION STATUS:\nCLEAN / PARTIALLY LOOP-CONTAMINATED / LOOP-CONTAMINATED\n\nORIGINAL ASK:\n\nACTUAL DELIVERABLE:\n\nFIRST VERIFIED LOOP POINT:\n\nPRIMARY FAILURE MECHANISM:\n\nASSUMPTIONS IMPLEMENTED BEFORE PROOF:\n\nVISIBLE OUTCOME AFTER 10 HOURS:\n\nTIME / COMPLEXITY INFLATION:\n\nSALVAGEABLE STATE:\n\nFIRST CIRCUIT BREAKER THAT SHOULD HAVE FIRED:\n\nFILES MODIFIED BY LUCE:\nNONE\n\nBUILD ACTIONS TAKEN:\nNONE\n\nNEXT ROUTE:\nDon + Coda\n\nANCHOR STATUS:\nFORENSIC RECON COMPLETE / INCOMPLETE\n\n==================================================\nHARD STOP\n==================================================\n\nTHIS IS AN AUTOPSY.\n\nDO NOT HEAL THE PATIENT.\n\nDO NOT BUILD THE NEXT VERSION.\n\nDO NOT WRITE THE FIX.\n\nDO NOT OPEN A NEW SLICE.\n\nRECONSTRUCT WHAT HAPPENED AND RETURN THE EVIDENCE TO DON.\n```"]}, "create_time": 1790364261.604945, "end_turn": true, "id": "1ad13301-0f3a-4783-a614-80db5d87482c", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "yqcjpd", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}}, "content_references": [], "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finish_details": {"stop_tokens": [200002], "type": "stop"}, "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab41b7c2620819187c626358eeb8a48", "is_complete": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "f1e0e61e-524a-4569-af83-c52b388fd2d3", "request_id": "b0a951e7-9fb0-491a-85c1-8ec2c29f501f", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "search_result_groups": [], "story_events": [], "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "4293e1f0-d971-447f-977b-eb778a9e1a81", "working_turn_id": "4293e1f0-d971-447f-977b-eb778a9e1a81"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790364322.744139, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "user"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content_type": "multimodal_text", "parts": [{"asset_pointer": "sediment://file_00000000d93c81fd991756fcbd5a0263", "content_type": "image_asset_pointer",