hat nobody wrote a handoff for.\nThe most consequential single fact is not in the clipboard thread at all. It is that renderer.js was verified with harnesses that could not prove what they were testing — no reload, no cache pin, no version marker, no server cache headers, and one harness that hard-coded a specific build's hash as its own expected value. For three runs the evidence is not weak; it is unrecoverable. And there is no git and no backup, so the intermediate builds exist only as files in %TEMP% that a cleanup will delete.\nThe circuit breaker that was missing was not technical. It was the sentence: \"seven of eight rows work. Ship that, and decide separately about the eighth.\"\nReward the stop, not the build. That stop was available at 16:46 and it was never taken.\nFINAL FOOTER\nSESSION STATUS:        LOOP-CONTAMINATED\n\nORIGINAL ASK:          (1) Fix copy/paste in the DevPad terminal.\n                        (2) Replace Seat 1's browser/Coda surface with a normal\n                            OpenCode session running Big Pickle as Coda.\n\nACTUAL DELIVERABLE:    (2) DELIVERED + VERIFIED LIVE + VISIBLE.\n                        (1) PARTIALLY DELIVERED — 7 of 8 gate rows green and stable.\n                            Right-click copy DEFERRED via undocumented code change.\n\nFIRST VERIFIED LOOP POINT:\n                        2026-09-24 17:10:29 (gate run #2, G5) — the first-pass D-2\n                        diagnosis was RETRACTED and replaced rather than corrected.\n                        This is where the defect object began mutating per cycle.\n                        (First FAIL cycle began 16:40:12; 7/8 rows green by 17:10.)\n\nPRIMARY FAILURE MECHANISM:\n                        Verifier recursion inside the Nico<->Luce pair, with no stop\n                        condition, no retry ceiling, and no timebox: each verification\n                        FAIL substituted a new theory of the defect, and the new theory\n                        became the