 Leica cameras, and it’s relatively compact. I’m seeing a current unlocked international listing around **$700**, which is a hell of a lot more rational than spending $1,200+ just to experiment with Xiaomi. citeturn608596product2\n\nThe **15T Pro** is the bigger/value-oriented option: 12 GB RAM, 512 GB storage, large 144 Hz AMOLED, and Leica camera hardware. Current global-version listings are roughly **$740–$900** depending on seller. citeturn608596product1turn608596product4\n\nThe **15 Ultra** is the lunatic-camera-phone option. Snapdragon 8 Elite, 16/512 GB, serious Leica camera system, but current global versions are around **$1,200+**. That feels excessive for what we’re trying to accomplish unless you specifically want the camera monster. citeturn608596product0\n\n### The T-Mobile question is the important part\n\nThe **global Xiaomi 15 Ultra** is actually encouraging: Xiaomi lists LTE bands **2/4/5/12/41/66/71** and 5G including **n25/n41/n66/n71**, among many others. Those are highly relevant T-Mobile bands. citeturn608596search0 Third-party compatibility data similarly shows the global 15 Ultra covering all seven of the LTE bands it tracks for T-Mobile and six of nine tracked 5G bands. citeturn608596search3\n\nBut band support ≠ carrier certification. **Before buying an imported Xiaomi, I would verify the exact IMEI with T-Mobile's BYOD checker**, because T-Mobile itself uses the IMEI/EID to determine whether a device can actually activate. citeturn608596search5\n\nAnd crucially: **buy GLOBAL, not Chinese-market firmware.** The global variants generally have materially better U.S. band coverage. For example, the global Xiaomi 15 supports more of T-Mobile's tracked 5G bands than the China model. citeturn608596search8\n\nMy target for us would therefore be:\n\n**Xiaomi 15 Global, 12 GB / 512 GB, unlocked — around $600–$700.**\n\nThat gives you the actual Xiaomi/HyperOS ecosystem, flagship hardware, and a fun connection to the same company whose **MiMo models we're using in GCE**, without spending Ultra money.\n\nAnd yes, there is something wonderfully GCE about **running MiMo on a Xiaomi while using the phone as the mobile front end to DevPad.** 😄"]}, "create_time": 1790217985.381345, "end_turn": true, "id": "2dba6174-8a25-482b-842e-878e47682a22", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "content_references": [{"alt": "([Mi Poland](https://www.mi.com/us?utm_source=chatgpt.com))", "end_idx": 479, "error": null, "fallback_items": null, "items": [{"attribution": "Mi Poland", "attribution_segments": null, "attributions": null, "hue": null, "pub_date": null, "refs": [{"ref_index": 1, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 0}, {"ref_index": 2, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 0}], "snippet": "", "supporting_websites": [{"attribution": "Mi Poland", "pub_date": null, "snippet": "", "title": "Xiaomi Global Home", "url": "https://www.mi.com/global/product-list/phone/?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}], "title": "Xiaomi United States | Xiaomi Official Website", "url": "https://www.mi.com/us?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}], "matched_text": "citeturn608596search1turn608596search2", "prefix": null, "prompt_text": null, "refs": [], "safe_urls": ["https://www.mi.com/global/product-list/phone/", "https://www.mi.com/global/product-list/phone/?utm_source=chatgpt.com", "https://www.mi.com/us", "https://www.mi.com/us?utm_source=chatgpt.com"], "start_idx": 437, "status": "done", "style": null, "type": "grouped_webpages"}, {"alt": "### [Xiaomi 15 5G Global / International](https://www.wirelessplace.com/products/xiaomi-15-5g-gsm-unlocked-international-version-new?utm_campaign=openai_catalog&utm_content=product_card&utm_medium=feed&variant=46753753071786&utm_source=chatgpt.com)\n*$699.50*\n\n### [Xiaomi 15T Pro Global](https://www.themobilemarvel.com/products/xiaomi-15t-pro-global-version?utm_campaign=openai_catalog&utm_content=product_card&utm_medium=feed&variant=47321270255875&utm_source=chatgpt.com)\n*$739.30*\n\n### [Xiaom