nce, durable design, and long battery life. Gamers and power users seeking top battery longevity should consider the Asus ROG Phone 9 Pro, which lasts over 20 hours but comes at a hefty $1,100. The Google Pixel 10 and iPhone 17 provide strong flagship performance at a more accessible $799, with the former excelling in AI tools and camera upgrades and the latter narrowing the gap with Apple’s Pro models. Samsung's Galaxy Z Fold 8 Ultra leads the foldable category with improved design and internals, despite its steep $2,099 starting price.", "thumbnail_url": "https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/lmJ5NVXkMtmFGlaThWIM7W4l7vWDkXOXIddWWc8BRQDkZB41b7RjKm3Nkf3-3bokrVp0hugprynHqgNPlraPBMhYYdXp2LDQ5w2BdzWt6DUww3KltIOBzLnJXvYJ7kb-", "title": "Best phones 2026 tested - our top picks", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://www.tomsguide.com/best-picks/best-phones"}, {"attribution": "www.tomsguide.com", "pub_date": 1790007623, "ref_id": {"ref_index": 13, "ref_type": "news", "turn_index": 743415}, "snippet": "As of 2026, gaming phones offer powerful alternatives to consoles and PCs, providing robust performance, long battery life, and high-refresh-rate displays for immersive gameplay. The Asus ROG Phone 9 Pro tops the list as the best overall gaming phone, with a 185Hz AMOLED display, Snapdragon 8 Elite chipset, exceptional 20:34 battery life, and gaming-specific features like AirTrigger controls and AniMe lights. For Android users wanting a flagship device with strong gaming credentials, the Samsung Galaxy S26 Ultra delivers with excellent GPU performance, efficient cooling, and powerful cameras. Meanwhile, the iPhone 18 Pro Max is the best gaming iPhone, offering the A20 Pro chip and impressive battery life, though with a heftier price tag. For value-conscious gamers, the RedMagic 11 Pro brings liquid and fan cooling and top-tier specs at a lower cost, albeit with weaker camera and dust resistance. Finally, the Galaxy Z Fold 7 offers a unique foldable experience with a large display and high-end internals, though at $2,000 it overdelivers for pure gaming needs. Overall, the best choice depends on user priorities such as OS, performance, budget, and additional features like photography or portability.", "thumbnail_url": "https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/3YBCBMfoBpyNpGm5vWKT_02-GdnjWkB5ZHVmQOv4it31Yb8XZCCr0eThXZatldRUs_gg1eAzWIh1GqA_WeZmGHZnumQQDJgwHnX4lcNj2mIRuIJt7rsCXVX9lAcQ9h1Z", "title": "The best gaming phone 2026 - I tested them all to crown a winner", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://www.tomsguide.com/best-picks/best-gaming-phones"}, {"attribution": "www.tomsguide.com", "pub_date": 1790003659, "ref_id": {"ref_index": 15, "ref_type": "news", "turn_index": 743415}, "snippet": "If you're in the market for a large smartphone, this guide highlights the best big phones of 2026, ideal for users who prioritize spacious displays, extended battery life, and top-tier performance. The best overall is the Samsung Galaxy S26 Ultra, boasting a 6.9-inch AMOLED screen, Snapdragon 8 Elite Gen 5 chip, and robust features like customizable privacy and AI tools. It stands out for exceptional performance and camera quality, despite minor drawbacks like its large camera bump.\n\nFor Apple fans, the iPhone 18 Pro Max also features a 6.9-inch display, A20 Pro chip, and superior battery life (18:27 hours), making it the top choice among big iPhones. It shines with strong performance, advanced camera capabilities, and fast charging, albeit with a higher price and heftier build.\n\nIf you're seeking flexibility, the foldable Motorola Razr Fold offers an expansive 8.1-inch inner screen and strong multitasking abilities. It supports up to four simultaneous apps and delivers solid battery life despite a few software hiccups.\n\nUltimately, Android offers more diversity in design and features, while iPhones provide tight ecosystem integration. Benchmarks and battery tests confirm these devices deliver premium user experiences for gaming, media, and productivity.", "thumbnail_url": "https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/WQcbFwnu7mIjYKutceSC59PdTXjMIR1nhgEf9SN-PvwasOrnW-99twhsD-ztDfB8M87V53PF_0Rct_nDhNG4DZSPgQIHGXVSH031LX-QUh_4V3HDvbglOketrYSKQ3Yk", "title": "I love big phones and I cannot lie - and here are the best you can buy right now", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://www.tomsguide.com/best-picks/best-big-phones"}, {"attribution": "www.tomsguide.com", "pub_date": 1789791300, "ref_id": {"ref_index": 16, "ref_type": "news", "turn_index": 743415}, "snippet": "The comprehensive comparison between the iPhone 18 Pro Max and Galaxy S26 Ultra reveals Apple’s flagship as the superior device in this seven-round face-off. Both phones debut at $1,299 and boast top-tier specs including 6.9-inch displays, powerful processors, and advanced camera systems. However, the iPhone pulls ahead in key categories. It features the A20 Pro chip, which outperforms Samsung’s Snapdragon 8 Elite Gen 5 in CPU and GPU benchmarks. The iPhone also excels in camera performance, particularly in low-light photography, with its innovative mechanical variable aperture. Battery life is another win for Apple, offering up to two hours more than Galaxy S26 Ultra. While Samsung leads in AI functionality and productivity, thanks to Galaxy AI, Privacy Display, and Samsung DeX, Apple counters with improved Siri AI integration and robust on-device intelligence. Both phones offer advanced software customization, but the iPhone’s fluid user experience, refined hardware design, and better dynamic range in photography deliver a more polished overall package. Despite Samsung's strengths, especially in AI automation and optical zoom, the iPhone 18 Pro Max is awarded the win for its performance, innovation, and reliability.", "thumbnail_url": "https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/F0zvSKfvAG985pFxT5WyO3gM1EMALgrOjGDavfZey_e6MpkiHSb86DQ31oInEYyhHW6eAcl1xzYX_D6vjIMU0NeIM5UlWuSgPBiHovhJ5QaOnHZBUwqNQ5HIzMb-InR7", "title": "I put the iPhone 18 Pro Max vs. Galaxy S26 Ultra through a 7-round face-off - here's the winner", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://www.tomsguide.com/phones/i-put-the-iphone-18-pro-max-vs-galaxy-s26-ultra"}], "type": "search_result_group"}, {"domain": "www.androidcentral.com", "entries": [{"attribution": "www.androidcentral.com", "pub_date": 1789677288, "ref_id": {"ref_index": 14, "ref_type": "news", "turn_index": 743415}, "snippet": "In 2026, flagship Android smartphones have significantly improved in water resistance, with devices now often earning IP68 or IP69 certifications for protection against water and dust. The top pick this year is the OnePlus 15, offering an IP69 rating, excellent gaming and camera performance, a large 7,300mAh battery, and competitive pricing at around $900. Budget-conscious buyers can opt for the Moto G Power 2026, which also features IP69 certification for under $300. Samsung’s Galaxy S26 Ultra remains the premium choice with advanced AI features, Privacy Display, and stellar overall performance. The Google Pixel 11 Pro leads in photography with powerful AI tools and a top-tier camera system, while the ASUS ROG Phone 9 Pro excels in battery life and gaming with its massive 5,800mAh battery and 185Hz display. For foldable device enthusiasts, the Samsung Galaxy Z Flip 8 is the top waterproof choice with an IP48 rating and enhanced durability. Though no phone is fully waterproof, ingress protection ratings ensure they handle most accidental water exposure. However, these ratings decline with wear, so users should still exercise caution.", "thumbnail_url": "https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/cJRhv9V-QE3yxBrHuU_gSheZYGLbFRF_UVdiDfJuTFFvoBjqe008XINXUVbTdAMiCTn6t9Tobwv0J7_t830_xLk3w3Hg3l9qY4as2lx6khU-LyPYBxLWPcRzQ5VDEoX0", "title": "Best waterproof phones 2026", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://www.androidcentral.com/best-waterproof-phone"}, {"attribution": "www.androidcentral.com", "pub_date": 1789746749, "ref_id": {"ref_index": 17, "ref_type": "news",