": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Exactly. If the requirement is **Snapdragon + RAM + battery + Android freedom**, then the camera tax is mostly dead weight.\n\nThe sweet spot is probably **not current flagship OnePlus** anymore. It’s either a prior-gen OnePlus or one of the performance-first Chinese/global phones.\n\n### The GCE-phone candidates I’d actually investigate\n\nproducts{\"selections\":[[\"turn743415product7\",\"OnePlus 13R 256GB Unlocked\"],[\"turn743415product15\",\"OnePlus 12 16GB/512GB\"],[\"turn743415product29\",\"Xiaomi POCO F7 Ultra Global 16GB/512GB\"],[\"turn743415product2\",\"REDMAGIC 10 Pro 16GB/512GB\"]]}\n\n**OnePlus 13R** is the sane-value baseline. It uses **Snapdragon 8 Gen 3**, has **12 GB RAM**, and I’m seeing an unlocked listing around **$490**. Qualcomm confirms the 13R is an 8 Gen 3 device. citeturn743415search3\n\n**OnePlus 12 16/512** is especially interesting if we find sane leftover or refurb pricing. Snapdragon 8 Gen 3 + **16 GB RAM / 512 GB** is already enough horsepower for a phone acting as a serious GCE terminal, SSH box, DevPad client, local tooling device, and multitasking monster.\n\nThen there’s the more Don-shaped option: **POCO F7 Ultra Global, 16/512**. That gives you the **Snapdragon 8 Elite**, LPDDR5X RAM and UFS 4 storage without pretending you’re buying a professional camera. Qualcomm lists the POCO F7 Ultra among Snapdragon 8 Elite devices, and current listings confirm the 16/512 configuration. citeturn743415search5\n\nAnd the absolute **“fuck the camera, give me compute”** phone is **REDMAGIC 10 Pro**: Snapdragon 8 Elite, **16 GB or even 24 GB RAM**, huge battery and active cooling. Android Authority specifically calls out its exceptional performance and cooling; it starts life much more like a handheld computer than a lifestyle phone. citeturn743415search2\n\nSo the hierarchy for **GCE Stack Phone**, not “best camera phone,” becomes:\n\n**$450–550:** OnePlus 13R — sensible, U.S.-friendly, fast enough.  \n**$500–700 if found well-priced:** OnePlus 12 16/512 — potentially the killer used/leftover value.  \n**~$650–800:** POCO F7 Ultra 16/512 — **8 Elite + 16 GB**, probably the spec/value target.  \n**~$750+**: REDMAGIC — only worth paying extra if we actually value sustained compute/cooling.\n\nAnd your instinct is right: **12 GB is my floor; 16 GB is the target.** For the thing you're describing—ChatGPT, Kimi/OpenCode terminals, SSH, browser tabs, remote desktop, DevPad, local scripts, potentially Termux—the extra RAM is far more valuable than paying for another ridiculous telephoto sensor.\n\nI’d specifically hunt **16 GB RAM / Snapdragon 8 Elite / global bands / <$650**. That is much closer to the spiritual successor of the old $300 OnePlus than spending $1,000 on modern flagship jewelry. memcite"]}, "create_time": 1790218066.080595, "end_turn": true, "id": "60135376-5e4c-4d24-ac18-0cdc36375c4a", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "content_references": [{"alt": "### [OnePlus 13R 256GB Unlocked](https://electronicsforce.com/products/oneplus-13r-256gb-unlocked-nebula-noir?utm_campaign=openai_catalog&utm_content=product_card&utm_medium=feed&variant=50261731016980&utm_source=chatgpt.com)\n*$489.99*\n\n### [OnePlus 12 16GB/512GB](https://inpexopcion.com/products/smartphone-oneplus-12-6-82-sim-doble-android-14-5g-usb-tipo-c-16-gb-512-gb-5400-mah-verde?utm_campaign=openai_catalog&utm_content=product_card&utm_medium=feed&variant=56540821225853&utm_source=chatgpt.com)\n*$678.39*\n\n### [Xiaomi POCO F7 Ultra Global 16GB/512GB](https://miot-store.com/products/hk-warehouse-xiaomi-poco-f7-ultra-global-16gb-512gb-in-screen-fingerprint-6-67-inch-xiaomi-hyperos-2-snapdragon-8-elite-octa-core-nfc-network-5g-black?utm_campaign=openai_catalog&utm_content=product_card&utm_medium=feed&variant=52709877317939&utm_source=chatgpt.com)\n*$801.55*\n\n### [REDMAGIC 10 Pro 16GB/512GB](https://saveoncells.com/products/redmagic-10-pro-global-nx789j-5