f Don is not authenticated, stop and let Don perform the browser login interactively.\n4. After login, preserve the browser profile/session so future DevPad launches reuse the authenticated state.\n5. Do not store Don’s password, session cookie, token, or credentials in DevPad config.\n6. Do not automate credential entry.\n7. Do not use incognito/private mode.\n8. Do not create a throwaway browser profile on every launch.\n\nBrowser choice:\n- Brave is acceptable.\n- Chrome is also acceptable.\n- Prefer whichever can be launched reliably with a dedicated persistent user-data/profile directory.\n\nSuggested implementation pattern:\n- Coda tile launches browser executable\n- Dedicated profile/user-data directory for Coda\n- Opens ChatGPT URL\n- Reuses same profile on future launches\n\nExample conceptual behavior:\nBrave/Chrome\n  -> persistent Coda browser profile\n  -> ChatGPT\n  -> Don manually logs in once if required\n  -> authenticated profile persists\n\nDo not:\n- scrape login credentials\n- store passwords\n- inject cookies\n- copy browser cookies from another profile\n- bypass authentication\n- hardcode OpenAI credentials\n- expose secrets in command-line arguments\n\nVerification:\nAfter Don completes login manually, verify:\n- Coda tile opens the intended browser\n- ChatGPT loads\n- Don is already authenticated on relaunch\n- browser profile persists across DevPad restart\n- Coda tile still points to the correct seat\n- no credentials are stored in DevPad files\n\nIf a browser login is required:\nSTOP at the login screen and tell Don:\n\"CODA BROWSER READY — MANUAL CHATGPT LOGIN REQUIRED\"\n\nDo not treat that as an implementation failure.\n\nFinal return:\n- Browser used\n- Persistent profile path\n- Launch command/config changed\n- Whether ChatGPT opened\n- Whether Don login is required\n- Whether authenticated state survived relaunch\n```\n\nThe important distinction for Nico is:\n\n**browser launch != authenticated Coda session**\n\nAnd yes, I would expect a **one-time browser login** to be part of the setup. After that, the dedicated Brave or Chrome profile should persist the session so you don’t have to keep logging in every time."]}, "create_time": 1790226864.611663, "end_turn": true, "id": "94a949b9-0b1f-4293-8657-be31118c8b64", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "hm4qe1", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}}, "content_references": [], "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finish_details": {"stop_tokens": [200002], "type": "stop"}, "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab41b7c2620819187c626358eeb8a48", "is_complete": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "e2d9ee3e-3feb-4366-9b22-a9a1a47f0649", "request_id": "e4884857-bfee-41a3-8133-b6f821880513", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "search_result_groups": [], "story_events": [], "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "bbc18fb7-8e70-4d79-b8d8-3219c47686ea", "working_turn_id": "bbc18fb7-8e70-4d79-b8d8-3219c47686ea"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790226886.172591, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "user"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Okay, that is, that is great. The other small tweak, we should buy the identity for these terminals so I could use my VoiceBridge to say number 1, number 2, number 3. "]}, "create_time": 1790226905.687, "end_turn": null, "id": "c2b6f5da-e98d-4de6-b497-f19dba09c71c", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "message_source": null, "request_id": "c38cbe77-9990-491b-af0c-19aff8450635", "selected_sources": [], "serialization_metadata": {"custom_symbol_offsets": []}, "turn_exchange_id": "5881e386-8b09-4dd8-ac85-f472754afb21", "working_turn_id": "5881e386-8b09-4dd8-ac85-f472754afb21"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_success