===========\nCURRENT FAILURE MODE\n==================================================\n\nThe Coda tile currently shows something like:\n\nseat: stopped\npid -\nhwnd -\n\neven though Don has successfully logged into ChatGPT in Brave.\n\nThis likely means the current browser-seat lifecycle logic is treating the browser like a terminal/service child process.\n\nThat is incorrect for browsers.\n\nChrome/Brave may:\n- reuse an already-running browser process\n- hand off the requested URL/profile to an existing process\n- cause the originally spawned launcher process to exit\n- create/reuse a window not directly owned by the initial spawned PID\n\nTherefore:\n\nSPAWNED CHILD PID ALIVE\nmust NOT be the only definition of browser seat = RUNNING.\n\n==================================================\nTARGET BROWSER-SEAT SEMANTICS\n==================================================\n\nFor Coda:\n\nRUNNING should mean:\n\nA matching Brave/Chrome browser window exists for the configured persistent profile / Coda launch target.\n\nTrack where practical:\n\n- browser executable\n- browser PID\n- top-level window handle / HWND\n- profile or user-data directory\n- target URL\n- running/stopped state\n\nDo not attempt to determine whether Don is authenticated by scraping cookies or account data.\n\nAuthentication remains Don-controlled inside the browser.\n\n==================================================\nLAUNCH BEHAVIOR\n==================================================\n\nCoda launch/focus should:\n\n1. Check for an existing matching browser window/session.\n2. If found:\n   - focus/activate that window\n   - do NOT launch a duplicate browser unnecessarily.\n3. If not found:\n   - launch Brave/Chrome using the persistent profile\n   - open https://chatgpt.com/\n   - discover the resulting browser window/process\n   - bind that result back to the Coda tile.\n\nUse the existing browser adapter if present.\n\nRepair the browser adapter rather than hardcoding browser logic into unrelated server paths.\n\n==================================================\nPERSISTENT PROFILE\n==================================================\n\nUse a persistent browser profile.\n\nPrefer one of:\n\nA. Don’s already-authenticated normal Brave profile\nOR\nB. a dedicated persistent Coda Brave profile that Don logs into once\n\nDo not:\n\n- store Don’s password\n- inject cookies\n- copy session cookies\n- scrape auth tokens\n- place credentials in config\n- place credentials in command-line arguments\n\nIf Don must log in once manually, that is acceptable.\n\nAfter Don logs in, the profile/session should persist naturally.\n\n==================================================\nDO NOT EMBED CHATGPT\n==================================================\n\nFor this pass:\n\nDo NOT:\n- iframe chatgpt.com\n- add Electron\n- add WebView2\n- add Chromium embedding\n- redesign DevPad around an embedded browser engine\n- proxy ChatGPT content\n- recreate ChatGPT UI\n\nThe Coda tile is a launcher/status/focus surface for the external authenticated browser.\n\nEmbedding can be revisited in a future architecture pass if Don still wants it.\n\n==================================================\nUI BEHAVIOR\n==================================================\n\nThe Coda tile should show something like:\n\n[1] Coda — ChatGPT\n\nBrowser: Brave\nStatus: RUNNING\nPID: <actual>\nHWND: <actual if available>\n\n[ Launch / Focus ]\n\nIf browser/window is unavailable:\n\nStatus: STOPPED\n\nIf launch succeeds but HWND cannot be determined:\n\nStatus: RUNNING\nHWND: UNKNOWN\n\nDo not mark STOPPED solely because the original spawned process exited if the actual browser window still exists.\n\n==================================================\nFOCUS BEHAVIOR\n==================================================\n\nLaunch / Focus must prioritize focus semantics.\n\nIf Coda browser is already open:\n- bring the correct browser window to foreground\n- do not spawn another instance\n\nIf no window exists:\n- launch it\n- then focus it\n\nIf Windows foreground restrictions prevent focus:\n- report the limitation clearly\n- do not silently spawn duplicates\n\n==================================================\nPROFILE / WINDOW MATCHING\n==================================================\n\nUse the cleanest available evidence to identify the Coda browser instance, such as:\n\n- configured executable\n- configured profile/user-data directory\n- command line\n- window title\n- process tree\n- HWND enumeration\n\nDo not bind Coda based only on:\n\n\"some chrome.exe exists\"\n\nor\n\n\"some brave.exe exists\"\n\nThe match must be specific enough to avoid focusing the wrong Don browser window.\n\n==================================================\nPRESERVE EXISTING DEVPAD FUNCTIONALITY\n==================================================\n\nDo not touch:\n\n- grid layout\n- inventory\n- VoiceBridge\n- OpenCode seat launchers\n- Kimi launchers\n- model binding work\n- seat doctrine\n- inbox MCP\n- numeric tile mapping\n\nThis is only the Coda browser-seat lifecycle fix.\n\n==================================================\nVERIFICATION\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n\n1. Brave/Chrome opens ChatGPT using the intended persistent profile.\n2. Don can authenticate manually if required.\n3. Close/restart DevPad without destroying the browser profile/session.\n4. Relaunch DevPad.\n5. Coda tile detects/focuses the existing browser session if still open.\n6. If browser is closed, Coda tile shows STOPPED.\n7. Press Launch / Focus.\n8. Browser launches correctly.\n9. Coda tile updates to RUNNING.\n10. PID is correct.\n11. HWND is correct if obtainable.\n12. Repeated focus does not create duplicate browser windows unnecessarily.\n\n==================================================\nSTOP CONDITIONS\n==================================================\n\nStop and return to Don if:\n\n- the existing browser adapter architecture cannot support external-window tracking cleanly\n- Brave requires invasive process/window hacks\n- correct profile matching cannot be made reliable\n- implementation would require Electron/WebView2/embedded Chromium\n- Windows focus behavior cannot be made reliable without a broader control layer\n\nDo not expand scope.\n\n==================================================\nREQUIRED RETURN\n==================================================\n\nRESULT:\nPASS / PARTIAL / BLOCKED\n\nBROWSER USED:\nBrave / Chrome\n\nPROFILE MODE:\nExisting Don profile / dedicated persistent Coda profile\n\nROOT CAUSE:\nExplain why Coda previously showed STOPPED.\n\nFILES CHANGED:\nExact files and purpose.\n\nLIVE STATE:\n- browser PID\n- HWND if available\n- target URL\n- Coda seat status\n\nVERIFICATION:\nExact checks performed.\n\nFINAL VERDICT:\nOne of:\n\nCODA EXTERNAL BROWSER SEAT READY\n\nCODA BROWSER READY — MANUAL CHATGPT LOGIN REQUIRED\n\nCODA BROWSER RUNNING — HWND/FOCUS LIMITATION REMAINS\n\nBLOCKED\n\nDo not continue into embedded-browser architecture after this pass.\n```\n\nThat’s the cleanest last-mile fix: **treat Coda as an external managed browser seat, not as an embedded web pane.**"]}, "create_time": 1790228859.770665, "end_turn": true, "id": "6bb26d6e-2bd5-49f9-8eba-ef137629d5a1", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "6qyst7", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}}, "content_references": [], "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finish_details": {"stop_tokens": [200002], "type": "stop"}, "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab41b7c2620819187c626358eeb8a48", "is_complete": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "6f1ec40e-b5ad-4d00-83bb-c0cd4f3c7481", "request_id": "f43f3ac2-05a0-4de4-bc9b-77ab636e83e1", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "search_result_groups": [], "story_events": [], "th