el_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "status": "running", "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "ea834b02-380f-4f5e-bae6-28e7c4d04930", "working_turn_id": "ea834b02-380f-4f5e-bae6-28e7c4d04930"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 0}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": "api_tool", "role": "tool"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content_type": "multimodal_text", "parts": ["Make sure to include fileciteturn2file0L5-L8 in your response to cite this file, or to surface it as a link. Replace the placeholder line range with the actual line range from the result that best fits the snippet you want to surface with the citation. If you cite multiple files, use a separate complete `filecite` marker for each file. Never put multiple `turnNfileM` targets inside a single `filecite` marker.\nUse ref_id \"turn2file0\" to reference this file. For broad questions or unknown locations, retrieve relevant chunks with `files.search` scoped to this file. Use `files.find` only for exact text, and use `files.read` for a known range or to expand relevant results. Full file size: 463 file lines.", "[L1] # myDon Control — Architecture Specification\n\n[L3] **Scope discipline:** This spec covers only the myDon Control orchestration pad and its integration seams with the existing DevPad Command Center. It does not redesign GCE, does not alter seat doctrine, does not bind models to seats, and does not introduce agent autonomy. Don routes; the system delivers.\n\n---\n\n[L7] ## 1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\n\n[L9] myDon Control is a thin, local, browser-based routing surface that gives Don a fast review-and-route loop over pending handoffs. The recommended architecture is **Option A**: a self-contained module *inside* the existing DevPad Command Center Node process, exposed as a separate route (`/mydon`) with its own API namespace (`/api/mydon/*`), its own file-backed event-sourced state store, and zero new infrastructure.\n\n[L11] Delivery flows through the **existing inbox/MCP lane** (no second messaging system). Seat resolution flows through the **existing seat registry** (no copy, no fork). Focus/ping flow through an in-process **DevPad UI control channel** (no terminal injection). VoiceBridge (Phase 4) converges on the same HTTP API — no parallel logic path.\n\n[L13] Doctrine is preserved structurally: the handoff schema contains **no model, provider, PID, or runtime fields in the routing path**. The seat is the routing identity; everything else is, at most, display metadata.\n\n---\n\n[L17] ## 2. RECOMMENDED ARCHITECTURE\n\n[L19] ### 2.1 Decision\n\n[L21] **Option A: embedded module + route in the existing Command Center server.**\n\n[L23] ### 2.2 Option comparison\n\n[L25] | | A — route/module in Command Center | B — separate local service | C — separate frontend, same API |\n[L26] |---|---|---|---|\n[L27] | Seat registry access | in-process, single source of truth | HTTP proxy to DevPad (fails when DevPad down) or **forked copy (doctrine violation)** | via API only |\n[L28] | Inbox/MCP delivery | in-process, reuses existing adapter | duplicate plumbing or proxy | via API only |\n[L29] | Focus/ping to DevPad UI | in-process WS, trivial | cross-process WS | via API only |\n[L30] | New port / process / auth surface | none | yes | one |\n[L31] | Lifecycle coupling | myDon UI dies with DevPad | survives DevPad restarts | dies with DevPad |\n[L32] | Build cost | lowest | highest | medium, no gain over A |\n\n[L34] **The decisive argument:** routing fundamentally depends on three things DevPad owns — seat registry, inbox delivery, and UI focus. A separate process would still depend on DevPad for all three, so separation buys almost nothing while adding a second control path, a second failure domain, and pressure to fork the registry (which would violate the doctrine). The only real benefit of B — \"view the queue while DevPad is down\" — is preserved anyway by the file-backed store: nothing is lost, only temporarily unviewable.\n\n[L36] **Mitigation for A's one real cost (process coupling):** myDon is structured as a module with a narrow injected context (`{ registry, inbox, wsBus, config }`). Extraction to a separate service later is a lift-and-shift of one directory, not a rewrite.\n\n[L38] ### 2.3 Key structural decisions\n\n[L40] 1. **Two stores, one delivery lane.** myDon owns a *routing queue store* (handoff records + lifecycle + audit). Seat inboxes (existing) remain the *delivery destination*. myDon never becomes a second inbox system.\n[L41] 2. **myDon is not a mandatory intermediary.** Sources that already know their target may write directly to a seat inbox via existing mechanisms. myDon is the surface for handoffs that *require Don's judgment* (unrouted, disputed, or Don-created). This prevents a bottleneck.\n[L42] 3. **Deterministic IDs** enable idempotent delivery and crash reconciliation (see §6, §9).\n[L43] 4. **Numeric tile aliases resolve through the registry.** `resolveSeat(ref)` accepts `\"luce\"`, `6`, or `\"6\"`. The 3×3 map is never hardcoded in myDon.\n\n---\n\n[L47] ## 3. COMPONENT DIAGRAM\n\n```\n[L50] +---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n[L51] |              GCE DevPad Command Center (Node.js, :4727)             |\n[L52] |                                                                     |\n[L53] |   +-------------------+        +----------------------------+      |\n[L54] |   | DevPad Board UI   |        | myDon UI  (served /mydon)  |      |\n[L55] |   | (work surface:    |        | queue view + 3x3 seat pad  |      |\n[L56] |   | terminals, panes) |        +-------------+--------------+      |\n[L57] |   +---------+---------+                      |                     |\n[L58] |             ^  WS: focus/ping/notify          | HTTP + WS           |\n[L59] |             |                                v                     |\n[L60] |   +---------+--------------------------------+-----------------+   |\n[L61] |   |              myDon module boundary                         |   |\n[L62] |   |                                                             |   |\n[L63] |   |   +----------------------+     +-------------------------+  |   |\n[L64] |   |   | Routing Service      |---->| seat-registry adapter  |  |   |\n[L65] |   |   | (/api/mydon/*)       |<----| (read-only projection)  |  |   |\n[L66] |   |   | route transaction    |     +-------------------------+  |   |\n[L67] |   |   | owner, idempotent    |---->| inbox/MCP adapter       |  |   |\n[L68] |   |   |                      |<----| (existing write path)   |  |   |\n[L69] |   |   |                      |     |  -> per-seat inboxes    |  |   |\n[L70] |   |   |                      |---->| devpad-control adapter  |  |   |\n[L71] |   |   |                      |<----| (focus / ping)           |  |   |\n[L72] |   |   +----------+-----------+     +-------------------------+  |   |\n[L73] |   |              |                                                |   |\n[L74] |   |   +----------v-----------+                                    |   |\n[L75] |   |   | Handoff State Store  |   JSONL event log; audit view     |   |\n[L76] |   |   +----------------------+   derives from the same log      |   |\n[L77] |   +-------------------------------------------------------------+   |\n[L78] |                                                                     |\n[L79] |   Seat runtimes read their own inboxes (existing behavior)          |\n[L80] +---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n\n[L82]   VoiceBridge (Phase 4) ---HTTP---> /api/mydon/*     (same contract,\n[L83]                                         no separate routing logic)\n```\n\n---\n\n[L88] ## 4. DATA FLOW\n\n[L90] ### 4.1 Happy path\n\n```\n[L93] (1) CREATE\n[L94]     source (seat runtime / Don / VoiceBridge / tool)\n        |\n[L96]         |  POST /api/mydon/handoffs\n        v\n[L98]     myDon queue [QUEUED]  --WS mydon:queue-->  UI shows it, badge++\n\n[L100] (2) ROUTE   (Don: select item, click ROUTE TO LUCE or press \"6\")\n        |\n[L102]         |  POST /api/mydon/handoffs/:id/route { targetSeat: \"luce\",\n[L103]         |                                        focus: true }\n        v\n[L105]     Routing Service\n[L106]         |-- (a) resolveSeat(\"luce\" | \"6\") ----> Seat Registry (read-only)\n[L107]         |-- (b) write handoff item -----------> Luce inbox\n[L108]         |        (deterministic id, returns inboxItemId)\n[L109]         |-- (c) append ROUTED event -----------> State Store (+ audit)\n[L110]         |-- (d) focus (optional) -------------> DevPad UI control\n[L111]                                                   -> tile 6 focused,\n[L112]                                                      pending badge++\n        v\n[L114]     myDon UI: item shows ROUTED -> auto-advance to next QUEUED item\n\n[L116] (3) CONSUME / ACK  (Phase 3)\n[L117]     Luce runtime reads inbox -> works\n        |\n[L119]         |  ACK write-back (inbox read receipt / status call)\n        v\n[L121]     [ACKNOWLEDGED] --(complete)--> [DONE]\n```\n\n[L124] ### 4.2 Failure branch (same flow, step b fails)\n\n```\n[L127]     (b) inbox write fails\n        |\n        v\n[L130]     append DELIVERY_FAILED event -> state [FAILED], error recorded\n[L131]     item stays visible, red, retryable. NO reroute, NO seat substitution.\n[L132]     (d) focus never runs; (c) records the failure for audit.\n```\n\n---\n\n[L137] ## 5. COMPONENT RESPONSIBILITIES\n\n[L139] ### myDon frontend (`/mydon`)\n[L140] - Render queue (ordered list + selected-item detail), 3×3 seat pad, filters, status bar.\n[L141] - Keyboard-first routing (see §10); click parity for every action.\n[L142] - All mutations go through `/api/mydon/*`; the frontend holds **no routing logic and no seat knowledge** beyond what `GET /api/mydon/seats` returns.\n[L143] - Does **not**: spawn processes, touch terminals, store seat data locally.\n\n[L145] ### Routing service (`/api/mydon/*`)\n[L146] - Sole owner of the route transaction, in strict order: (1) append `route_started`, (2) inbox write, (3) append `routed`. This ordering plus deterministic IDs gives crash-recoverability (§9).\n[L147] - Enforces idempotency (same-seat re-route = no-op; different-seat re-route = 409).\n[L148] - Enforces routability (service/utility seat classes rejected).\n[L149] - Does **not**: consult models, providers, PIDs, window order, or runtime state when routing. Does **not** auto-select or auto-retry targets. Does **not** silently substitute seats.\n\n[L151] ### Seat registry (existing, read-only from myDon)\n[L152] - Source of truth for seat identity, tile-number aliases, seat class (`work | service | utility`), inbox address.\n[L153] - myDon's adapter adds only `resolveSeat(ref)` — a lookup, never a copy. Registry changes (seat list, tile numbers) propagate to myDon automatically.\n\n[L155] ### Inbox / MCP adapter (existing)\n[L156] - `writeHandoffItem(seat, item)` — writes the structured handoff into the target seat's inbox; returns the inbox item ID.\n[L157] - Preferred: supports client-supplied IDs (upsert-by-id) so duplicates collapse. (Open question #1, §16.)\n[L158] - Phase 3: expose read receipts for ACK write-back.\n\n[L160] ### DevPad control adapter\n[L161] - `focusTile(seat)` — sends a UI command over the existing WS channel to the DevPad frontend (highlight tile, switch view). A **UI action, not terminal input**.\n[L162] - `ping(seat)` — Phase 3: trigger inbox refresh + visible indicator.\n[L163] - `wake()` — explicitly **out of scope for V1**. No process spawning from myDon.\n[L164] - Does **not**: inject keystrokes into terminals unless the runtime later supports a safe control message (and only then, by explicit decision).\n\n[L166] ### VoiceBridge adapter (Phase 4)\n[L167] - Maps voice intents → existing `/api/mydon/*` calls (see §11). Holds no routing logic of its own.\n\n[L169] ### Handoff state store\n[L170] - Append-only JSONL event log + in-memory projection rebuilt on start; periodic snapshot compaction.\n[L171] - **The audit trail is the event log** — no separate audit store to drift out of sync.\n\n---\n\n[L175] ## 6. HANDOFF DATA MODEL\n\n[L177] ```json\n{\n[L179]   \"handoffId\": \"hdo_01JT8Z3M4K9Q\",     // ULID: unique + sortable\n[L180]   \"seq\": 41,                            // short human ordinal (\"handoff 41\")\n[L181]   \"source\": {\n[L182]     \"type\": \"seat\",                     // seat | don | voicebridge | tool\n[L183]     \"seat\": \"nico\",                     // null if not a seat\n[L184]     \"tile\": 4                           // informational only\n  },\n[L186]   \"subject\": \"Verify DevPad model binding\",\n[L187]   \"context\": \"Short summary or full context block. Hard cap: 16 KB.\",\n[L188]   \"project\": \"GCE_DevPad_Command_Center\",\n[L189]   \"workstream\": null,\n[L190]   \"priority\": \"normal\",                 // low | normal | high | urgent\n[L191]   \"suggestedTargetSeat\": \"luce\",        // ADVISORY ONLY — Don decides\n[L192]   \"targetSeat\": null,                   // set at route time\n[L193]   \"status\": \"queued\",\n[L194]   \"delivery\": {                         // filled by routing service\n[L195]     \"attemptedAt\": null,\n[L196]     \"deliveredAt\": null,\n[L197]     \"inboxItemId\": null,                // = \"mydon-<handoffId>\" (deterministic)\n[L198]     \"attempts\": 0,\n[L199]     \"lastError\": null\n  },\n[L201]   \"focus\": {\n[L202]     \"requested\": false,\n[L203]     \"succeeded\": null,\n[L204]     \"error\": null\n  },\n[L206]   \"ack\": { \"at\": null, \"via\": null },   // Phase 3\n[L207]   \"attachments\": [\n[L208]     { \"kind\": \"path\", \"value\": \"C:\\\\...\\\\binding-report.md\" }\n  ],\n[L210]   \"tags\": [],\n[L211]   \"viewedAt\": null,                      // UI metadata, not lifecycle state\n[L212]   \"createdAt\": \"2026-02-14T10:22:31Z\",\n[L213]   \"routedAt\": null,\n[L214]   \"routedBy\": null,                      // \"don\" | \"voicebridge:don\"\n[L215]   \"updatedAt\": \"...\"\n}\n```\n\n[L219] **Schema rules (doctrine enforcement):**\n\n[L221] 1. **No `model`, `provider`, `runtime`, or `pid` fields.** Validation rejects them. Current runtime/model info may appear on the *seat projection* (`GET /api/mydon/seats`) as display-only data, never in the handoff routing path.\n[L222] 2. **Deterministic inbox item ID** (`mydon-<handoffId>`) — the same handoff routed twice to the same seat produces one inbox item wherever the inbox honors client IDs; where it cannot, the routing service guards by state.\n[L223] 3. **Attachments by reference only** (paths, URLs). No file contents, no credentials, no cookies, no tokens in payloads.\n[L224] 4. Two identifiers on purpose: `handoffId` (machine, collision-proof) and `seq` (human/voice: \"hold 41\").\n\n---\n\n[L228] ## 7. API CONTRACT\n\n[L230] All endpoints local-only (bound to 127.0.0.1), JSON in/out, namespaced under `/api/mydon` to avoid collision with existing DevPad endpoints. `seatRef` = seat name or numeric tile alias, resolved via registry.\n\n[L232] | Method | Path | Purpose | Phase |\n[L233] |---|---|---|---|\n[L234] | GET | `/api/mydon/handoffs` | List queue; filters: `status`, `project`, `priority` | 1 |\n[L235] | POST | `/api/mydon/handoffs` | Create handoff (any source) | 1 |\n[L236] | GET | `/api/mydon/handoffs/:id` | Fetch one + audit summary | 1 |\n[L237] | POST | `/api/mydon/handoffs/:id/route` | `{ targetSeat, focus? }` — idempotent | 1 (focus: 2) |\n[L238] | POST | `/api/mydon/handoffs/:id/hold` | QUEUED → HELD | 1 |\n[L239] | POST | `/api/mydon/handoffs/:id/resume` | HELD → QUEUED | 1 |\n[L240] | POST | `/api/mydon/handoffs/:id/retry` | FAILED → QUEUED | 1 |\n[L241] | POST | `/api/mydon/handoffs/:id/complete` | → DONE (manual close) | 3 |\n[L242] | GET | `/api/mydon/seats` | Seat projection: name, tile, class, availability (display-only), inbox depth | 1 |\n[L243] | POST | `/api/mydon/seats/:seatRef/focus` | Focus the seat's DevPad tile | 2 |\n[L244] | POST | `/api/mydon/seats/:seatRef/ping` | Inbox refresh + indicator | 3 |\n[L245] | GET | `/api/mydon/audit` | Query events (`handoffId`, `seat`, `since`) | 1 |\n\n[L247] **Conventions:**\n[L248] - Error envelope: `{ \"error\": { \"code\", \"message\", \"details\" } }`. Codes: `SEAT_UNKNOWN`, `SEAT_NOT_ROUTABLE`, `ALREADY_ROUTED`, `VALIDATION`, `INBOX_WRITE_FAILED`, `DEVPAD_UNAVAILABLE` (non-fatal when route-without-focus was requested).\n[L249] - WS topics on the existing bus: `mydon:queue` (queue changed), `mydon:result` (action outcome), `mydon:ui` (Phase 4 voice navigation).\n[L250] - Route is **idempotent**: re-POST with the same `targetSeat` on a ROUTED handoff returns `200` with current state; a different `targetSeat` returns `409 ALREADY_ROUTED` (no silent rerouting).\n\n---\n\n[L254] ## 8. STATE MACHINE\n\n[L256] Six states, one deliberate simplification from the brief: **NEW and PENDING collapse into `QUEUED`**. \"Seen by Don\" is recorded as `viewedAt` metadata (an event in the log), not a lifecycle state — read/unread is UI semantics, and a distinct NEW→PENDING transition would add an ambiguous state with no behavioral difference. All six intended meanings remain reachable.\n\n```\n[L259]               hold                  resume\n[L260]    QUEUED <--------------> HELD\n     |  ^                            \n[L262]      |  +---- retry ---- FAILED\n     |                     \n[L264]      | route (ok)              \n     v                     \n[L266]    ROUTED --ack (seat, P3)--> ACKNOWLEDGED --complete--> DONE\n[L267]      \\------------------------- complete (manual) --------^\n```\n\n[L270] | From | Event | To | Guard / note |\n[L271] |---|---|---|---|\n[L272] | QUEUED | route | ROUTED | seat resolves to routable class **and** inbox write confirmed |\n[L273] | QUEUED | route | FAILED | inbox write fails; `delivery.lastError` recorded; item stays visible |\n[L274] | FAILED | retry | QUEUED | manual only |\n[L275] | QUEUED | hold | HELD | never lost; surfaced via HELD filter |\n[L276] | HELD | resume | QUEUED | |\n[L277] | ROUTED | route (same seat) | ROUTED | no-op, 200 |\n[L278] | ROUTED | route (other seat) | — | 409, rejected |\n[L279] | ROUTED | ack | ACKNOWLEDGED | seat-side write-back (Phase 3) |\n[L280] | ROUTED / ACKNOWLEDGED | complete | DONE | Don or seat |\n\n[L282] Retraction of a mis-routed handoff (Phase 2+ candidate): implemented as a *correction handoff* to the same seat, never silent deletion.\n\n---\n\n[L286] ## 9. FAILURE HANDLING\n\n[L288] | Failure | Behavior | Recovery |\n[L289] |---|---|---|\n[L290] | Unknown / unroutable seat (`SEAT_UNKNOWN`, service/utility class) | 400; handoff stays QUEUED, untouched | Don picks another seat |\n[L291] | Inbox write fails | Append `delivery_failed`; state FAILED with error text; item stays visible in red | Retry → QUEUED → route. **Never** auto-reroute or substitute a seat |\n[L292] | DevPad UI not connected (no WS client) | Route still succeeds — delivery is decoupled from UI liveness; `focus.succeeded=false` recorded | Focus-retry button; auto re-focus on reconnect |\n[L293] | Focus times out / errors | Route unaffected; warning icon on the item | Manual re-focus |\n[L294] | Duplicate click / double-send, same seat | Idempotent no-op (200); deterministic inbox ID prevents a second inbox item wherever inbox honors client IDs; server-side in-flight lock per `handoffId` guards the rest | — |\n[L295] | Route to different seat after ROUTED | 409 `ALREADY_ROUTED`; original routing stands | Create a correction handoff (P2+) |\n[L296] | **Crash between inbox write and log write** | On restart: any handoff with `route_started` but no `routed` is *reconciled* — probe the target inbox for `mydon-<handoffId>`; found → mark ROUTED; absent → revert to QUEUED | Automatic; deterministic IDs make this a lookup, not a guess |\n[L297] | Store write fails before inbox write | Route aborted with 500 before any side effect (ordering guarantees this) | Retry |\n[L298] | Target runtime offline | **Irrelevant to routing** — the inbox is durable; the seat reads on next activation | None needed; only ACK timing shifts |\n\n[L300] Two hard invariants: **(1) no silent rerouting or seat substitution; (2) a failed route always leaves the handoff visible and retryable.**\n\n---\n\n[L304] ## 10. UI STRUCTURE\n\n[L306] Single compact page. The interaction cadence — CLICK → SEND → NEXT — is implemented as **route + auto-advance**: after a successful route, selection moves to the next QUEUED item automatically.\n\n```\n[L309] +--------------------------------------------------------------------+\n[L310] | myDon        QUEUED 7  HELD 2  FAILED 1      [filters]   connected |\n[L311] +--------------------------------------------+-----------------------+\n[L312] | QUEUE  (j/k navigate, Enter = route to     |  SEAT PAD             |\n[L313] |        suggested target)                  |  [1 Coda  ][2 Chiave] |\n[L314] | ----------------------------------------- |  [3 Vittorio]         |\n[L315] | > hdo 41  Verify DevPad model binding     |  [4 Nico  ][5 VoiceB*]|\n[L316] |           from nico -> sugg LUCE    high  |  [6 Luce  ]           |\n[L317] |   hdo 40  Draft port notes                |  [7 Talon ][8 Keel  ] |\n[L318] |           from don  -> sugg TALON  normal |  [9 Falcon]           |\n[L319] |   hdo 39  ...                            |  -------------------  |\n[L320] |                                           |  FOCUS INBOX STATUS   |\n[L321] | SELECTED hdo 41                           |  Route+Focus = Shift+# |\n[L322] |   context ...  project ...  created ...   |  (* service seat:     |\n[L323] |   [ROUTE TO LUCE]  [HOLD h]               |     not routable)     |\n[L324] +--------------------------------------------+-----------------------+\n[L325] | last: hdo 40 -> Talon (routed, focused)                            |\n[L326] +--------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```\n\n[L329] **Keyboard map (Don's speed loop):**\n\n[L331] | Key | Action |\n[L332] |---|---|\n[L333] | `j` / `k` or arrows | next / previous queue item |\n[L334] | `1`–`9` | route selected handoff to that seat (registry-resolved) |\n[L335] | `Shift+1`–`Shift+9` | route + focus |\n[L336] | `Enter` | route to `suggestedTargetSeat` (if set) |\n[L337] | `h` | hold |\n[L338] | `r` | retry FAILED item |\n\n[L340] Rules: suggested target tile is pre-highlighted; VoiceBridge tile renders distinctly and is not clickable for routing; utility seats (future Bedrock Mantle / Kimi ad hoc row) render dimmed, non-routable; a small composer (\"New handoff\", source = don, optional current-pane reference) covers the *current-context send* case. Target: **under 5 seconds per item** through the queue via keyboard.\n\n---\n\n[L344] ## 11. VOICEBRIDGE FUTURE HOOK\n\n[L346] **Convergence rule:** VoiceBridge maps intents to the *same* HTTP endpoints and the shared `mydon:ui` WS topic. It never calls adapters directly and never contains routing logic. If a voice command and a click produce different event logs, that's a bug.\n\n[L348] | Voice intent | Call |\n[L349] |---|---|\n[L350] | \"send this to Luce\" / \"route this to number 6\" | `POST /api/mydon/handoffs/:selected/route { targetSeat }` |\n[L351] | \"send and next\" | same, then advance via `mydon:ui` topic |\n[L352] | \"hold this\" | `POST .../hold` |\n[L353] | \"next handoff\" | `mydon:ui` navigation topic |\n[L354] | \"focus number 4\" / \"open Nico\" | `POST /api/mydon/seats/4/focus` |\n[L355] | \"new handoff, subject ...\" | `POST /api/mydon/handoffs` (dictated fields) |\n[L356] | \"mark done\" | `POST .../complete` |\n\n[L358] Numeric voice targets (\"route to 6\") flow through `resolveSeat()` exactly like a clicked tile — muscle memory and registry authority share one code path.\n\n---\n\n[L362] ## 12. SECURITY BOUNDARIES\n\n[L364] - **Loopback only.** Server binds 127.0.0.1; same-origin serving of `/mydon` avoids CORS entirely. If a token ever becomes necessary (e.g., to fence other local processes), a simple bearer token in a user-only-readable file is the ceiling — nothing heavier.\n[L365] - **No secrets anywhere in myDon's path:** no passwords, cookies, API keys, or tokens — not in the store, not in payloads, not in command lines. Attachments are references only.\n[L366] - **No shell execution.** myDon never spawns processes (WAKE is out of scope for V1); it never injects terminal input in V1.\n[L367] - **No authority from runtime identity.** Model/provider/PID never appear in the routing path — they are not stored on handoffs at all. This closes an entire class of authority-confusion failures by construction.\n[L368] - **No silent failure.** Failed routes stay visible with errors; no rerouting, no substitution, no auto-retry.\n[L369] - **Audit = append-only log,** trivially inspectable in a text editor. Tamper-evidence is out of scope for the local trust model.\n[L370] - VoiceBridge inherits all boundaries by construction — it can do only what the API allows.\n\n---\n\n[L374] ## 13. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\n[L376] | Phase | Scope | Acceptance criteria |\n[L377] |---|---|---|\n[L378] | **1 — Queue + Route** | Module scaffold; store (JSONL + projection); schema + validation; `POST/GET /handoffs`, `route/hold/resume/retry`; seats projection; minimal UI (queue + seat pad + keyboard); audit view | Create → route → item **present in target seat's inbox** with deterministic ID; failed write leaves item FAILED and visible; process restart preserves queue; same-seat re-route is a no-op |\n[L379] | **2 — Route + Focus** | DevPad control channel `focusTile`; Route+Focus action; pending badge on target tile; focus results recorded on handoff | Route+Focus focuses the correct tile in a running DevPad; with DevPad closed, route succeeds and focus is recorded failed + retryable |\n[L380] | **3 — Ping / Status / ACK** | `ping` (inbox refresh + indicator); seat-side ACK write-back; `complete`; inbox depth in seat pad; filters | ACK flips ROUTED → ACKNOWLEDGED; audit shows the full chain create→route→ack→done |\n[L381] | **4 — Voice** | VoiceBridge intent adapter onto the same API + `mydon:ui` topic | \"Route to 6\" produces byte-identical audit events to clicking route-to-6 |\n\n[L383] Each phase ships independently usable value; Phase 1 alone already replaces manual routing.\n\n---\n\n[L387] ## 14. FILE / MODULE STRUCTURE\n\n```\n[L390] C:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother\\GCE_DON\\command-center\\\n  src\\\n[L392]     mydon\\                        <-- one self-contained module boundary\n[L393]       index.js                    entry: registerMydon(server, context)\n[L394]       api.js                      HTTP handlers, namespace /api/mydon\n[L395]       routing-service.js          route transaction, idempotency, reconcile\n[L396]       store.js                    JSONL event log, projection, compaction\n[L397]       schema.js                   handoff validation (rejects model/provider fields)\n[L398]       bus.js                      WS topics: mydon:queue, mydon:result, mydon:ui\n[L399]       adapters\\\n[L400]         seat-registry.js          read-only resolveSeat(ref) over existing registry\n[L401]         inbox.js                  writeHandoffItem() over existing inbox/MCP path\n[L402]         devpad-control.js         focusTile / ping over existing UI control WS\n[L403]       public\\\n[L404]         index.html  mydon.js  mydon.css\n  data\\\n[L406]     mydon\\\n[L407]       handoffs-YYYYMM.jsonl       monthly event log partitions\n[L408]       snapshot.json               compacted projection\n```\n\n[L411] **Placement rules:** `context` is injected by the Command Center (`{ registry, inbox, wsBus, config }`) — myDon never reaches around it. Data lives under the existing `data/` root so backups cover it. If Option B extraction is ever justified, `src/mydon/` + `data/mydon/` move as a unit. Adapt `src/` nesting to the Command Center's actual layout; the *boundary* is the requirement, not the exact tree.\n\n---\n\n[L415] ## 15. TEST PLAN\n\n[L417] | # | Test | Proves |\n[L418] |---|---|---|\n[L419] | 1 | Unit: state machine — every legal and illegal transition pair | Lifecycle correctness |\n[L420] | 2 | Unit: `resolveSeat(\"luce\")`, `resolveSeat(6)`, `resolveSeat(\"6\")` resolve identically; unknown → error; service/utility → `SEAT_NOT_ROUTABLE` | Numeric-alias-through-registry doctrine |\n[L421] | 3 | Unit: schema rejects/strips `model`, `provider`, `pid` fields | MODEL ≠ SEAT enforced at the boundary |\n[L422] | 4 | Integration: create → route → assert inbox item exists with deterministic ID, state ROUTED, audit events present | Happy path end-to-end |\n[L423] | 5 | Integration: double-route same seat → one inbox item; different seat → 409 | Idempotency, no silent reroute |\n[L424] | 6 | Failure injection: inbox adapter throws → FAILED retained, retry succeeds | Failure visibility and recovery |\n[L425] | 7 | Focus failure: no WS client connected → route succeeds, `focus.succeeded=false` | Delivery/UI decoupling |\n[L426] | 8 | Crash recovery: inject `route_started` without `routed`; restart; assert reconciliation (ROUTED if inbox item exists, QUEUED if not) | The two-write problem is solved |\n[L427] | 9 | Durability: hard process kill, restart, queue intact | Local-first reliability |\n[L428] | 10 | Manual UX: keyboard loop timing (<5s/item); Phase 4 voice-vs-click audit parity | The actual product goal |\n\n---\n\n[L432] ## 16. RISKS / OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n[L434] 1. **Inbox capabilities** — Does the existing inbox/MCP support client-supplied item IDs (clean dedupe), read receipts (ACK), and delete/retract? These determine whether idempotency needs the full server-side guard and how Phase 3 ACK is wired.\n[L435] 2. **Unrouted pool** — Does the existing inbox already have a pending/unrouted pool that should feed the myDon queue as the single entry door? Recommended: yes, ingest it rather than requiring sources to learn a new endpoint.\n[L436] 3. **DevPad UI control channel** — Does `focusTile` exist, or does the DevPad frontend need a small addition? What are the multi-window semantics? (Raising the OS browser window may be blocked; V1 should focus *within* DevPad only.)\n[L437] 4. **VoiceBridge seat class** — Confirm it is registered as `service`, non-routable, rendered distinctly.\n[L438] 5. **Numeric alias governance** — Changing the tile map breaks muscle memory; make it an explicit registry change requiring a note. myDon never edits the map, only reads it.\n[L439] 6. **Queue hygiene** — HELD items accumulate silently; add an aging indicator and a periodic review ritual. Volume is unknown; JSONL scales comfortably to thousands.\n[L440] 7. **Context limits** — Enforce the 16 KB cap and reference-only attachments, or large payloads will bloat seat inboxes.\n[L441] 8. **Utility row** — Bedrock Mantle / Kimi ad hoc tiles enter the registry as `utility`, non-routable by default — confirming routing-by-registry rather than layout.\n[L442] 9. **Multiple myDon tabs** — Server is the authority; WS pushes keep tabs consistent. Low risk, noted for completeness.\n[L443] 10. **Exit condition for Option B** — If DevPad downtime becomes routine and Don needs queue access during it, the module boundary makes extraction cheap. Until then, don't pay the cost.\n\n---\n\n[L447] ## 17. FINAL RECOMMENDATION\n\n[L449] **Build myDon Control as Option A: an embedded module with its own route, API namespace, and store inside the existing DevPad Command Center.**\n\n[L451] Concretely:\n\n[L453] - Serve the UI at **`/mydon`** on the existing `:4727` server.\n[L454] - Expose **`/api/mydon/*`** as the single control contract — used by the UI now and by VoiceBridge in Phase 4.\n[L455] - Keep the **JSONL event-sourced store** under `data/mydon/` — durable, debuggable, and the audit trail in one artifact.\n[L456] - Deliver through the **existing inbox/MCP adapter**; resolve through the **existing seat registry**; focus through an **in-process WS control message** — never terminal injection.\n[L457] - Keep the module boundary clean enough that extraction to a separate service is a directory move, not a redesign.\n\n[L459] And equally concretely, what **not** to do: no second seat registry, no second messaging system, no model/provider anywhere in the routing path, no autonomous routing or retry, no process spawning, no heavyweight infrastructure. A local Node module is sufficient, and sufficiency is the architecture.\n\n[L461] The result is exactly the target loop, with Don's authority structural rather than procedural:\n\n[L463] **DON SEES THE HANDOFF → DON CLICKS THE TARGET (or says it, or keys it) → HANDOFF ROUTES BY SEAT → TARGET INBOX RECEIVES IT → DEVPAD FOCUSES/PINGS THE RIGHT SEAT → DON IS ALREADY ON THE NEXT ITEM.**"]}, "create_time": 1790228937.7938907, "end_turn": null, "id": "52a3df7c-a7e8-4464-a3a1-24f3495d7df5", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "chime_version": 1, "classifier_response": "default", "command": "context_stuff", "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab41b7c2620819187c626358eeb8a48", "is_visually_hidden_from_conversation": false, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "parent_id": "0e7978c8-f59a-4f29-99c6-86fd4fa09c44", "reasoning_start_time": 1790228937.6504443, "request_id": "0afcc118-f99a-4e9a-907e-863d520a1ecc", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "retrieval_file_index": 0, "retrieval_turn_number": 2, "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "ea834b02-380f-4f5e-bae6-28e7c4d04930", "working_turn_id": "ea834b02-380f-4f5e-bae6-28e7c4d04930"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": "api_tool", "role": "tool"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["All the files uploaded by the user have been fully loaded. You can still search connectors to find additional information."]}, "create_time": 1790228937.8131983, "end_turn": null, "id": "caa92ace-2fb0-422e-8297-281cc82ce734", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "chime_version": 1, "classifier_response": "default", "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab41b7c2620819187c626358eeb8a48", "is_visually_hidden_from_conversation": false, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "parent_id": "52a3df7c-a7e8-4464-a3a1-24f3495d7df5", "reasoning_start_time": 1790228937.6504443, "request_id": "0afcc118-f99a-4e9a-907e-863d520a1ecc", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "ea834b02-380f-4f5e-bae6-28e7c4d04930", "working_turn_id": "ea834b02-380f-4f5e-bae6-28e7c4d04930"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content_type": "thoughts", "source_analysis_msg_id": "16189c12-a760-462c-a630-399648affe63", "thoughts": [{"chunks": [], "content": "I’m broadly approving the architecture, especially embedded routing and one delivery lane. Before building, I’d resolve the duplicate-queue risk, clarify handoff ownership, and ensure the controller feels distinct despite sharing the existing server.", "finished": true, "summary": "Reviewing the GLM spec"}, {"chunks": [], "content": "", "finished": true, "summary": "Reviewed the GLM specification"}]}, "create_time": 1790228947.593696, "end_turn": false, "id": "2f0b8515-07ca-4909-9199-3b9b13b1cbba", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "chime_version": 1, "citations": [], "classifier_response": "default", "content_references": [], "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": false, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "disable_turn_actions": true, "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab41b7c2620819187c626358eeb8a48", "hide_inline_actions": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "16189c12-a760-462c-a630-399648affe63", "reasoning_start_time": 1790228937.6504443, "reasoning_status": "is_reasoning", "request_id": "0afcc118-f99a-4e9a-907e-863d520a1ecc", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "skip_reasoning_title": "Skip", "summary_type": "raw_cot", "thinking_effort": "standard", "tool_icons": [], "turn_exchange_id": "ea834b02-380f-4f5e-bae6-28e7c4d04930", "working_turn_id": "ea834b02-380f-4f5e-bae6-28e7c4d04930"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content": "Worked for 12s", "content_type": "reasoning_recap"}, "create_time": 1790228950.751617, "end_turn": false, "id": "e2dda35c-5ffa-4b80-b9cb-53ec1ca15f69", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": false, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finished_duration_sec": 12, "hide_inline_actions": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "2f0b8515-07ca-4909-9199-3b9b13b1cbba", "reasoning_end_time": 1790228950.630551, "reasoning_recap_type": "hide_all", "reasoning_start_time": 1790228937.6504443, "reasoning_status": "reasoning_ended", "request_id": "0afcc118-f99a-4e9a-907e-863d520a1ecc", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "ea834b02-380f-4f5e-bae6-28e7c4d04930", "working_turn_id": "ea834b02-380f-4f5e-bae6-28e7c4d04930"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Yeah — **GLM did a very good job here.** This is not generic architecture fluff; it understood the operating model and gave us something buildable.\n\nMy assessment: **accept the architecture direction, but make a few corrections before we hand it to Nico.**\n\nThe strongest decision is **Option A**: make myDon a logically separate control surface at `/mydon`, but run it inside the existing Command Center backend on `:4727`. That preserves the distinction we wanted — **Main DevPad = work surface, myDon = orchestration surface** — without creating another server, registry, inbox implementation, or port. fileciteturn2file0L21-L36\n\n## What GLM got exactly right\n\nThe control path is clean:\n\n**myDon → routing service → seat registry → existing inbox/MCP → DevPad focus/ping**\n\nIt explicitly keeps the model/provider/PID out of routing authority, which is essential. Seat identity remains the stable key. fileciteturn2file0L9-L13\n\nIt also nailed the user interaction we were describing:\n\n**CLICK → SEND → NEXT**\n\nwith numeric routing, keyboard shortcuts, and auto-advance to the next queued item. The proposed `1–9` route and `Shift+1–9` route+focus model is especially good for Don muscle memory. fileciteturn2file0L304-L340\n\nAnd I really like this architectural distinction:\n\n- **route succeeds even if focus fails**\n- runtime being offline does **not** invalidate delivery\n- handoff lives durably in the inbox until that seat returns\n\nThat prevents UI/session health from corrupting workflow state. fileciteturn2file0L286-L300\n\n## The one thing I would challenge before building\n\nGLM proposes **two stores**:\n\n1. myDon routing queue/event store\n2. existing seat inboxes\n\nThat can be correct, but I don't want Nico building a new event-sourced queue until he first inspects what our **existing `ai-inbox` / queue / inbox MCP** already provides.\n\nGLM itself recognizes this uncertainty: it asks whether the existing inbox already has an unrouted/pending pool and recommends ingesting that rather than forcing everyone through a new entry mechanism. fileciteturn2file0L432-L441\n\nSo my correction would be:\n\n> **Recon the existing inbox first. Reuse it as the pending queue if it already provides sufficient durable identity/status. Create `data/mydon/` only for state the existing inbox genuinely cannot represent.**\n\nOtherwise we risk creating:\n\n**inbox queue → myDon queue → target inbox**\n\nwhen what we really need may simply be:\n\n**existing inbox queue → Don routes → target inbox**\n\nThat's even cleaner.\n\n## Second correction: separate surface, shared process\n\nI would retain GLM's Option A but be explicit about UX.\n\n`/mydon` should feel like another application even though it shares the backend:\n\n**Main window**\n`http://localhost:4727/`\n\n**Controller window**\n`http://localhost:4727/mydon`\n\nThat gives Don exactly the thing we envisioned: a little dedicated control pad sitting alongside the big terminal wall.\n\nEventually we could even have:\n\n```text\n[ Main DevPad ]        [ myDon Controller ]\n\nwork surface           orchestration surface\nterminals               queue\nruntime status          route\nidentity                handoffs\nlive work               focus/ping\n```\n\nSame control plane underneath.\n\n## Third correction: don't overbuild event sourcing yet\n\nThe JSONL event model is technically sound. I like deterministic IDs, idempotency, explicit failure, and auditability. fileciteturn2file0L169-L171\n\nBut **monthly logs + snapshots + compaction + crash reconciliation** may be more machinery than v1 needs.\n\nI would preserve the invariants:\n\n- deterministic handoff ID\n- route exactly once\n- same-seat repeat is idempotent\n- different-seat repeat gets rejected\n- failed delivery stays visible\n- audit record exists\n\nBut let Nico choose the smallest implementation compatible with the existing inbox.\n\nIf JSONL falls naturally out of what already exists, great.\n\nDon't create a miniature event-sourcing platform because GLM drew one.\n\n## Fourth correction: focus/ping comes after routing proof\n\nGLM's phase sequence is already sensible:\n\n1. Queue + Route\n2. Route + Focus\n3. Ping / Status / ACK\n4. Voice\n\nfileciteturn2file0L374-L381\n\nI would hold that hard.\n\nThe first acceptance test should be ridiculously simple:\n\n> Don sees one pending handoff → clicks Luce → Luce's existing inbox receives the exact structured artifact → myDon says ROUTED → next item selected.\n\nOnce that is green, **then** wire focus.\n\nThat protects us from another situation where we spend hours on Windows focus/HWND bullshit before proving the actual product.\n\n## One thing GLM gave us that I definitely want to keep\n\nThis schema rule:\n\n> **No model, provider, runtime, or PID fields in the routing path.**\n\nfileciteturn2file0L219-L224\n\nExcellent.\n\nThe UI can absolutely show:\n\n**Luce — Big Pickle — OpenCode — LIVE**\n\nbut the route itself remains:\n\n**targetSeat = luce**\n\nThat means tomorrow we swap Big Pickle for MiMo and **nothing in myDon routing changes**.\n\nThat's exactly our doctrine implemented in code instead of just written in a document.\n\n## My final disposition\n\n**Architecture: ACCEPT WITH MINOR CORRECTIONS.**\n\nI would freeze these principles:\n\n**myDon `/mydon` = separate Don-facing UI**  \n**same `:4727` backend = shared control plane**  \n**existing seat registry = sole routing authority**  \n**existing inbox/MCP = delivery lane**  \n**existing pending inbox/queue reused before creating a second queue**  \n**route first, focus second, ping third, voice fourth**  \n**Don always makes the routing decision**  \n**seat identity survives all model/runtime changes**\n\nAnd yes — **wait for Nico to finish the current DevPad correction before starting this build.** We don't want him touching runtime bindings and introducing `/mydon` simultaneously.\n\nOnce current DevPad is stable, this architecture is ready to turn into a **Nico implementation brief**."]}, "create_time": 1790228937.792675, "end_turn": true, "id": "0890c787-167f-45e5-988b-6dc8bc6dac5f", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [{"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 635, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "files/context_stuff", "authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "52a3df7c-a7e8-4464-a3a1-24f3495d7df5", "cited_message_idx": 227, "cloud_doc_url": null, "doi": null, "effective_time": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_6ed2b5b2a848819196aee1ce7ebe2b34", "line_range": [21, 36], "publication_year": null, "retrieval_file_index": 0, "retrieval_turn": 2, "run_id": null, "search_result_idx": null, "set_id": null, "source_icon_url": null, "source_label": null, "source_url": null, "spl_version": null, "title": null}, "id": "file_00000000d65c81fd98a7dd90b5c907cb", "name": "Pasted markdown.md", "source": "my_files", "text": "**Option A: embedded module + route in the existing Command Center server.**\n### 2.2 Option comparison\n| | A — route/module in Command Center | B — separate local service | C — separate frontend, same API |", "type": "file"}, "start_ix": 606}, {"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 937, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "files/context_stuff", "authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "52a3df7c-a7e8-4464-a3a1-24f3495d7df5", "cited_message_idx": 227, "cloud_doc_url": null, "doi": null, "effective_time": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_6ed2b5b2a848819196aee1ce7ebe2b34", "line_range": [9, 13], "publication_year": null, "retrieval_file_index": 0, "retrieval_turn": 2, "run_id": null, "search_result_idx": null, "set_id": null, "source_icon_url": null, "source_label": null, "source_url": null, "spl_version": null, "title": null}, "id": "file_00000000d65c81fd98a7dd90b5c907cb", "name": "Pasted markdown.md", "source": "my_files", "text": "...\nmyDon Control is a thin, local, browser-based routing surface that gives Don a fast review-and-route loop over pending handoffs. The recommended architecture is **Option A**: a self-contained module *inside* the existing DevPad Command Center Node process, exposed as a separate route (`/mydon`) with its own API namespace (`/api/mydon/*`), its own file-backed event-sourced state store, and zero new infrastructure.\nDelivery flows through the **existing inbox/MCP lane** (no second messaging system). Seat resolution flows through the **existing seat registry** (no copy, no fork). Focus/ping flow through an in-process **DevPad UI control channel** (no terminal injection). VoiceBridge (Phase 4) converges on the same HTTP API — no parallel logic path.\nDoctrine is preserved structurally: the handoff schema contains **no model, provider, PID, or runtime fields in the routing path**. The seat is the routing identity; everything else is, at most, display metadata.", "type": "file"}, "start_ix": 909}, {"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 1237, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "files/context_stuff", "authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "52a3df7c-a7e8-4464-a3a1-24f3495d7df5", "cited_message_idx": 227, "cloud_doc_url": null, "doi": null, "effective_time": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_6ed2b5b2a848819196aee1ce7ebe2b34", "line_range": [304, 340], "publication_year": null, "retrieval_file_index": 0, "retrieval_turn": 2, "run_id": null, "search_result_idx": null, "set_id": null, "source_icon_url": null, "source_label": null, "source_url": null, "spl_version": null, "title": null}, "id": "file_00000000d65c81fd98a7dd90b5c907cb", "name": "Pasted markdown.md", "source": "my_files", "text": "## 10. UI STRUCTURE\nSingle compact page. The interaction cadence — CLICK → SEND → NEXT — is implemented as **route + auto-advance**: after a successful route, selection moves to the next QUEUED item automatically.\n+--------------------------------------------------------------------+", "type": "file"}, "start_ix": 1206}, {"citation